{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TnrCszSUWar6VkiMttzXro","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/packet_loop.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Bundle of types and entry points implementing quic's\n4\t//! reference event loop (`sockloop.c`) on top of the [`socks`]\n5\t//! UDP shims.  The loop:\n6\t//!\n7\t//! * owns one or more [`SocketCtx`] per network family,\n8\t//! * polls them with [`socks::select`] (or `select`/\n9\t//!   `WSAWaitForMultipleEvents` in the C original),\n10\t//! * routes received datagrams into quic, and\n11\t//! * fires application callbacks ([`PacketLoopCbFn`]) at\n12\t//!   well-defined points (loop ready, after recv, after send,\n13\t//!   address change, time check, system-call duration spike, wake-up,\n14\t//!   alt-port).\n15\t//!\n16\t//! Three layered entry points cover the same loop with different\n17\t//! parameter shapes:\n18\t//!\n19\t//! * [`run`] — the original 1.x signature, preserved for\n20\t//!   compatibility.  Builds a [`LoopParam`] on the stack and forwards.\n21\t//! * [`run_v2`] — takes a [`LoopParam`] directly.\n22\t//! * [`NetworkThreadCtx::run`] — takes a fully-populated\n23\t//!   [`NetworkThreadCtx`]; the threaded entry point.\n24\t//!\n25\t//! Plus the threading helpers ([`NetworkThreadCtx::spawn`] et al.)\n26\t//! that wrap `pthread_create` / `CreateThread`.\n27\t//!\n28\t//! Phase 4 fills the event-loop, thread-management, server-context,\n29\t//! and socket-opening bodies against the safe Rust socket abstraction.\n30\t//!\n31\t//! [`socks`]: crate::socks\n32\t//!\n33\t//! ## Pointer-shape decisions\n34\t//!\n35\t//! Read from `quic/sockloop.c`, `quic/winsockloop.c`, and\n36\t//! the demo callers in `first/demo.c`,\n37\t//! `sample/sample_*.c`, and `test/sockloop_test.c`:\n38\t//!\n39\t//! * `Quic*` parameters are non-null in every observed\n40\t//!   caller — they translate to `&mut Quic`.\n41\t//! * `LoopParam*` is *borrowed* by the loop\n42\t//!   helpers (the caller stack-allocates it in\n43\t//!   `run_v2` / the demo apps) — `&mut` here.  Inside\n44\t//!   [`NetworkThreadCtx`] the same pointer is *owned*\n45\t//!   when `is_param_allocated == 1` ([`Config::start_server_threads`]\n46\t//!   `malloc`s a copy and `delete_network_thread` `free`s\n47\t//!   it).  Phase 1 keeps the field as `Option<Box<…>>` and folds\n48\t//!   the C `is_param_allocated` flag away — the `Box` itself\n49\t//!   carries ownership; borrowed-param call sites store `None`\n50\t//!   plus a separate borrow at runtime.\n51\t//! * `picoquic_quic_config_t*` is borrowed-mut by\n52\t//!   [`Quic::create_server`] and [`Config::start_server_threads`]\n53\t//!   (they read and may mutate fields like `ticket_encryption_key`).\n54\t//! * Function-pointer typedefs (`packet_loop_cb_fn`,\n55\t//!   `custom_thread_create_fn`, `_setname_fn`,\n56\t//!   `_delete_fn`) become traits per the Phase 1 rules; the C `void*\n57\t//!   callback_ctx` companion folds into the trait implementor's\n58\t//!   state.  The C `(cb_mode, void* callback_argv)` tagged-union\n59\t//!   pair becomes the typed [`LoopEvent`] enum — each variant\n60\t//!   carries the payload type the C `cb_mode` implied.\n61\t//! * `SocketCtx* s_ctx` is used as both a single object\n62\t//!   ([`SocketCtx::close`]) and a fixed-size array\n63\t//!   ([`open_sockets`] writes up to `PACKET_LOOP_SOCKETS_MAX`\n64\t//!   entries).  The single-object path is a method on [`SocketCtx`];\n65\t//!   the array path takes `&mut [SocketCtx]`, with the slice length\n66\t//!   subsuming the C convention of \"callee writes and returns the count\".\n67\t//! * `NetworkThreadCtx**` outputs from\n68\t//!   [`Config::start_server_threads`] become `&mut [Option<Box<…>>]`\n69\t//!   — the slice carries `nb_threads_max`; each slot is filled with\n70\t//!   `Some` on success.\n71\t//! * Bitfields collapse to `bool`s.  Single-bit C `int : 1` /\n72\t//!   `unsigned int : 1` flag fields don't justify `bitflags!` on a\n73\t//!   set of unrelated booleans (see `config.rs` for the\n74\t//!   established convention).\n75\t//! * `volatile int` fields in [`NetworkThreadCtx`]\n76\t//!   become plain `i32` / `bool` — `Send`/`Sync` is out of v1 scope,\n77\t//!   so the volatile semantics have nowhere to land.\n78\t//! * `sockaddr_storage` fields fold into `Option<SocketAddr>`,\n79\t//!   matching the [`socks`] convention (`AF_UNSPEC` ↔ `None`).\n80\t//! * The Windows-only fields (`overlap`, `WSARecvMsg`, `WSASendMsg`,\n81\t//!   `dataBuf`, `msg`, …) and the io_uring fields are dropped per\n82\t//!   the v1 single-target scope.\n83\t//! * `recv_buffer: uint8_t* + recv_buffer_size: size_t` is an\n84\t//!   owning pair (allocated in `packet_set_windows_socket`\n85\t//!   on the Windows path, or `packet_loop_recv_buf_uring_init`\n86\t//!   on io_uring; freed in [`SocketCtx::close`]).\n87\t//!   On the canonical Linux/`select` build neither is used — every\n88\t//!   datagram lands in the shared loop buffer.  The field shape is\n89\t//!   `Option<Vec<u8>>` so the unused state is `None`; Vec subsumes\n90\t//!   the (pointer, size) pair into one owning value.\n91\t\n92\tuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n93\t\n94\tuse std::thread::JoinHandle;\n95\t\n96\tuse crate::Error;\n97\tuse crate::Instant;\n98\tuse crate::config::Config;\n99\tuse crate::errors::InternalError;\n100\tuse crate::socks::{EcnCodepoint, OsError, RecvInfo, Socket};\n101\tuse crate::{AlpnSelect, Quic, StreamDataCallback};\n102\t\n103\tconst AF_INET: i32 = 2;\n104\tconst AF_INET6: i32 = 10;\n105\tconst EIO: i32 = 5;\n106\tconst PACKET_LOOP_DELAY_MAX: i64 = 10_000_000;\n107\t\n108\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n109\t// Compile-time limits.\n110\t\n111\t/// Maximum number of UDP sockets a single packet loop can drive at\n112\t/// once (one per address family, optionally times two for the\n113\t/// public/private port split).  C: `PACKET_LOOP_SOCKETS_MAX`.\n114\tpub const PACKET_LOOP_SOCKETS_MAX: usize = 4;\n115\t\n116\t/// Maximum datagrams pulled from one socket per loop iteration.\n117\t/// C: `PACKET_LOOP_RECV_MAX`.\n118\tpub const PACKET_LOOP_RECV_MAX: usize = 10;\n119\t\n120\t/// Maximum datagrams pushed to one socket per loop iteration.\n121\t/// C: `PACKET_LOOP_SEND_MAX`.\n122\tpub const PACKET_LOOP_SEND_MAX: usize = 10;\n123\t\n124\t/// Hard cap on how long the loop will wait between iterations\n125\t/// (microseconds).  C: `PACKET_LOOP_SEND_DELAY_MAX`.\n126\tpub const PACKET_LOOP_SEND_DELAY_MAX: u64 = 2500;\n127\t\n128\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n129\t// Per-socket context.\n130\t\n131\t/// State the loop maintains per UDP socket.  C: `socket_ctx_t`.\n132\t///\n133\t/// Trimmed to the canonical Linux build: the Windows\n134\t/// (`WSAOVERLAPPED`, `WSARecvMsg`, …) and io_uring (`msghdr`,\n135\t/// `iovec`, `ctrl_buffer`) fields are dropped per the v1\n136\t/// single-target scope.  The four C bitfields collapse to plain\n137\t/// `bool` flags.\n138\tpub struct SocketCtx<S: crate::socks::Socket> {\n139\t    /// OS socket handle.  `None` mirrors the C `INVALID_SOCKET`\n140\t    /// sentinel for \"not yet open\".  Generic over the active\n141\t    /// `Socket` implementation; the default in production is\n142\t    /// `crate::socks_socket2::Socket2Udp` (wraps `socket2::Socket`).\n143\t    pub fd: Option<S>,\n144\t    /// Address family the socket was opened in (`AF_INET`,\n145\t    /// `AF_INET6`).  Stays `i32` to match call sites that pass the\n146\t    /// libc `AF_*` constants directly.\n147\t    pub af: i32,\n148\t    /// Port number the socket is bound to (host byte order).\n149\t    pub port: u16,\n150\t    /// `htons(port)` cached so the loop can stamp it into received\n151\t    /// destination addresses without a per-packet byte-swap.\n152\t    pub n_port: u16,\n153\t    /// Private port number — the port reserved for this thread when\n154\t    /// the public port is shared with siblings (see\n155\t    /// `is_port_shared`).  C: `private_port`.\n156\t    pub private_port: u16,\n157\t    /// Whether this socket is bound to a port shared with other\n158\t    /// threads (e.g., port 443 across an H3 thread pool — uses\n159\t    /// `SO_REUSEPORT`).  C: `int is_port_shared : 1`.\n160\t    pub is_port_shared: bool,\n161\t    /// Whether [`open_sockets`]-equivalent setup has completed\n162\t    /// for this socket.  C: `unsigned int is_started : 1`.\n163\t    pub is_started: bool,\n164\t    /// Whether the kernel honored `UDP_SEGMENT` (GSO) on this\n165\t    /// socket.  C: `unsigned int supports_udp_send_coalesced : 1`.\n166\t    pub supports_udp_send_coalesced: bool,\n167\t    /// Whether the kernel honored `UDP_GRO` on this socket.\n168\t    /// C: `unsigned int supports_udp_recv_coalesced : 1`.\n169\t    pub supports_udp_recv_coalesced: bool,\n170\t    /// Owning receive buffer.  Used only on the Windows-async and\n171\t    /// io_uring paths; the canonical Linux build leaves it as\n172\t    /// `None` and uses the shared loop buffer instead.\n173\t    /// C: `uint8_t* recv_buffer` plus the `recv_buffer_size`\n174\t    /// companion (length is implicit in the slice).\n175\t    pub recv_buffer: Option<Box<[u8]>>,\n176\t    /// Source address of the most recent datagram (`recvmsg`'s\n177\t    /// `msg_name`).  C: `struct sockaddr_storage addr_from` plus\n178\t    /// `from_length` — `Option<SocketAddr>` carries both.\n179\t    pub addr_from: Option<SocketAddr>,\n180\t    /// Destination address parsed out of `IP_PKTINFO` /\n181\t    /// `IPV6_PKTINFO` for the most recent datagram.\n182\t    /// C: `struct sockaddr_storage addr_dest` + `dest_length`.\n183\t    pub addr_dest: Option<SocketAddr>,\n184\t    /// Receiving interface index (from the same cmsg).\n185\t    /// C: `int dest_if`.\n186\t    pub dest_if: i32,\n187\t    /// `IP_TOS` / `IPV6_TCLASS` ECN code-point on the most recent\n188\t    /// datagram.  C: `unsigned char received_ecn`.\n189\t    pub received_ecn: u8,\n190\t    /// Number of bytes read into the loop buffer on the most recent\n191\t    /// recv.  C: `int bytes_recv` (C uses `-1` for error; the Rust\n192\t    /// loop propagates errors through `Result` at the call site and\n193\t    /// only writes a valid byte count here).\n194\t    pub bytes_recv: usize,\n195\t    /// Scratch space for assembling outbound `cmsg` payloads\n196\t    /// (`IP_PKTINFO`, `IPV6_PKTINFO`, `UDP_SEGMENT`).\n197\t    /// C: `char cmsg_buffer[1024]`.\n198\t    pub cmsg_buffer: [u8; 1024],\n199\t    /// `UDP_GRO` segment size on the most recent datagram (the\n200\t    /// kernel's `UDP_GRO` cmsg).  C: `size_t udp_coalesced_size`.\n201\t    pub udp_coalesced_size: usize,\n202\t}\n203\t\n204\timpl<S: crate::socks::Socket> Default for SocketCtx<S> {\n205\t    fn default() -> Self {\n206\t        SocketCtx {\n207\t            fd: None,\n208\t            af: 0,\n209\t            port: 0,\n210\t            n_port: 0,\n211\t            private_port: 0,\n212\t            is_port_shared: false,\n213\t            is_started: false,\n214\t            supports_udp_send_coalesced: false,\n215\t            supports_udp_recv_coalesced: false,\n216\t            recv_buffer: None,\n217\t            addr_from: None,\n218\t            addr_dest: None,\n219\t            dest_if: 0,\n220\t            received_ecn: 0,\n221\t            bytes_recv: 0,\n222\t            cmsg_buffer: [0; 1024],\n223\t            udp_coalesced_size: 0,\n224\t        }\n225\t    }\n226\t}\n227\t\n228\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n229\t// Callback enum + companion arg structs.\n230\t\n231\t/// Loop-callback event delivered to [`PacketLoopCbFn::callback`].\n232\t/// Replaces the C `(packet_loop_cb_enum cb_mode, void* callback_argv)`\n233\t/// pair: the enum carries the per-event payload directly, so\n234\t/// implementors no longer cast a `void*`.\n235\t/// C: `packet_loop_cb_enum`.\n236\t#[derive(Debug)]\n237\tpub enum LoopEvent<'a> {\n238\t    /// Loop has finished initializing.  C: `packet_loop_ready`,\n239\t    /// `callback_argv: *mut LoopOptions`.\n240\t    Ready(&'a mut LoopOptions),\n241\t    /// Number of packets received this iteration.  C:\n242\t    /// `packet_loop_after_receive`, `callback_argv: *mut size_t`.\n243\t    AfterReceive(usize),\n244\t    /// Number of packets sent this iteration.  C:\n245\t    /// `packet_loop_after_send`, `callback_argv: *mut size_t`.\n246\t    AfterSend(usize),\n247\t    /// New local address advertised by the application after a\n248\t    /// port update.  C: `packet_loop_port_update`,\n249\t    /// `callback_argv: *mut sockaddr`.\n250\t    PortUpdate(core::net::SocketAddr),\n251\t    /// Optional check-in fired when the application set\n252\t    /// [`LoopOptions::do_time_check`].  C:\n253\t    /// `packet_loop_time_check`.\n254\t    TimeCheck(&'a mut TimeCheckArg),\n255\t    /// Optional system-call duration report fired when the\n256\t    /// application set [`LoopOptions::do_system_call_duration`].\n257\t    /// C: `packet_loop_system_call_duration`.\n258\t    SystemCallDuration(&'a mut SystemCallDuration),\n259\t    /// Wake-up event triggered by [`NetworkThreadCtx::wake_up`].\n260\t    /// C: `packet_loop_wake_up` with `callback_argv: NULL`.\n261\t    WakeUp,\n262\t    /// Alt-port address surfaced for multipath / migration tests.\n263\t    /// C: `packet_loop_alt_port`.\n264\t    AltPort(core::net::SocketAddr),\n265\t}\n266\t\n267\t/// System-call duration statistics surfaced through the optional\n268\t/// [`LoopEvent::SystemCallDuration`] callback.\n269\t/// C: `packet_loop_system_call_duration_t`.\n270\t#[derive(Debug, Default, Copy, Clone)]\n271\tpub struct SystemCallDuration {\n272\t    /// Duration of the most recent zero-delay system call\n273\t    /// (microseconds).\n274\t    pub scd_last: u64,\n275\t    /// Maximum observed system-call duration so far.\n276\t    pub scd_max: u64,\n277\t    /// Smoothed system-call duration (RFC-6298–style EWMA).\n278\t    pub scd_smoothed: u64,\n279\t    /// Mean absolute deviation around `scd_smoothed`.\n280\t    pub scd_dev: u64,\n281\t}\n282\t\n283\t/// In/out argument for the [`LoopEvent::TimeCheck`] callback.\n284\t/// The loop fills `current_time` and a proposed `delta_t`;\n285\t/// the application overwrites `delta_t` with a (possibly smaller)\n286\t/// value if it has work to do sooner.\n287\t/// C: `packet_loop_time_check_arg_t`.\n288\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone)]\n289\tpub struct TimeCheckArg {\n290\t    /// Loop-time timestamp.\n291\t    pub current_time: Instant,\n292\t    /// Proposed sleep, in microseconds — application may shrink.\n293\t    pub delta_t: i64,\n294\t}\n295\t\n296\timpl Default for TimeCheckArg {\n297\t    fn default() -> Self {\n298\t        Self {\n299\t            current_time: Instant::from_ticks(0),\n300\t            delta_t: 0,\n301\t        }\n302\t    }\n303\t}\n304\t\n305\t/// Application callback fired at the lifecycle and per-iteration\n306\t/// events listed in [`LoopEvent`].\n307\t///\n308\t/// C: `int (*packet_loop_cb_fn)(picoquic_quic_t* quic,\n309\t/// packet_loop_cb_enum cb_mode, void* callback_ctx, void*\n310\t/// callback_argv)`.  The `callback_ctx` companion folds into the\n311\t/// trait implementor's state; the `(cb_mode, callback_argv)` tagged\n312\t/// union folds into [`LoopEvent`].\n313\t///\n314\t/// Returns `Ok(())` on success, or an error to break the loop.\n315\tpub trait PacketLoopCbFn {\n316\t    fn callback(&mut self, quic: &mut Quic, event: LoopEvent<'_>) -> Result<(), Error>;\n317\t}\n318\t\n319\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n320\t// Loop options + parameters.\n321\t\n322\t/// Feature-flags the application advertises in response to the\n323\t/// [`LoopEvent::Ready`]\n324\t/// callback.  C: `packet_loop_options_t`, three single-bit\n325\t/// `unsigned int : 1` fields collapsed to `bool` per the\n326\t/// established convention (see `config.rs`).\n327\t#[derive(Debug, Default, Copy, Clone)]\n328\tpub struct LoopOptions {\n329\t    /// Application wants the loop to call back with\n330\t    /// [`LoopEvent::TimeCheck`]\n331\t    /// before each select.\n332\t    pub do_time_check: bool,\n333\t    /// Application wants notifications when zero-delay system calls\n334\t    /// take noticeably long.\n335\t    pub do_system_call_duration: bool,\n336\t    /// Application provides an alternate port for migration /\n337\t    /// multipath testing.\n338\t    pub provide_alt_port: bool,\n339\t}\n340\t\n341\t/// Loop-construction parameters (v2 / v3 entry points).\n342\t/// C: `packet_loop_param_t`.  `repr(C)` is dropped — the\n343\t/// struct never crosses an external boundary.\n344\t#[derive(Debug, Default, Copy, Clone)]\n345\tpub struct LoopParam {\n346\t    /// Default port for outgoing connections.  `0` ⇒ ephemeral.\n347\t    pub local_port: u16,\n348\t    /// `AF_INET` / `AF_INET6`, or `0` for \"both\".\n349\t    pub local_af: i32,\n350\t    /// Outbound interface index (or `0` to leave it to the kernel).\n351\t    pub dest_if: i32,\n352\t    /// Server / public-facing port.  `0` for client-only loops.\n353\t    pub public_port: u16,\n354\t    /// Whether the public port is shared across this thread pool\n355\t    /// (uses `SO_REUSEPORT`).\n356\t    pub is_port_shared: bool,\n357\t    /// `SO_SNDBUF` / `SO_RCVBUF` size, or `0` to skip the syscall.\n358\t    pub socket_buffer_size: i32,\n359\t    /// Disable `UDP_SEGMENT` GSO even if the kernel advertises it.\n360\t    pub do_not_use_gso: bool,\n361\t    /// Open the public-port socket pair too (needed for migration).\n362\t    pub extra_socket_required: bool,\n363\t    /// When both port pairs exist, prefer the extra socket as the\n364\t    /// outgoing source.\n365\t    pub prefer_extra_socket: bool,\n366\t    /// Inject a synthetic `EIO` once into the send path (debug\n367\t    /// hook).\n368\t    pub simulate_eio: bool,\n369\t    /// Cap on the size of an individual coalesced send.  `0` ⇒\n370\t    /// kernel default.\n371\t    pub send_length_max: usize,\n372\t}\n373\t\n374\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n375\t// Custom thread-management hooks.\n376\t\n377\t/// Spawn-a-thread hook.  C:\n378\t/// `int (*custom_thread_create_fn)(void** thread_id,\n379\t/// thread_fn thread_fn, void* arg)`.\n380\t///\n381\t/// In C, `(thread_fn, arg)` is the trampoline + state pair the new\n382\t/// thread will run.  In Rust, [`std::thread::spawn`] already takes\n383\t/// an arbitrary `FnOnce() + Send` closure (which subsumes the C\n384\t/// \"function pointer + void* arg\" pattern), so the hook reduces to\n385\t/// \"produce a [`JoinHandle`] from that closure\".\n386\tpub trait CustomThreadCreateFn {\n387\t    /// Create a thread that runs `thread_fn` to completion.  The\n388\t    /// returned [`JoinHandle`] is owned by the caller and passed\n389\t    /// back through [`CustomThreadDeleteFn::delete`] at teardown.\n390\t    ///\n391\t    /// The C contract returns `0` for success / non-zero `errno`\n392\t    /// otherwise; the [`OsError`] payload carries the same value\n393\t    /// that the C `*ret` out-parameter would on\n394\t    /// [`NetworkThreadCtx::spawn_custom`].\n395\t    fn create(\n396\t        &mut self,\n397\t        thread_fn: Box<dyn FnOnce() + Send + 'static>,\n398\t    ) -> Result<JoinHandle<()>, OsError>;\n399\t}\n400\t\n401\t/// Set-thread-name hook.  C:\n402\t/// `void (*custom_thread_setname_fn)(char const* thread_name)`.\n403\t///\n404\t/// Length is capped at 16 bytes (including the trailing NUL) on\n405\t/// Linux's `prctl(PR_SET_NAME, …)`; the trait takes a `&str` slice\n406\t/// and lets the implementor truncate / re-encode as needed.\n407\tpub trait CustomThreadSetnameFn {\n408\t    /// Apply `thread_name` to the *current* thread.  Called from\n409\t    /// inside the thread after it starts, per the C convention.\n410\t    fn set_name(&mut self, thread_name: &str);\n411\t}\n412\t\n413\t/// Tear-down-a-thread hook.  C:\n414\t/// `void (*custom_thread_delete_fn)(void** thread_id)`.\n415\t///\n416\t/// In Rust the standard `JoinHandle` cleans itself up on drop, so\n417\t/// this hook only matters for backends that allocate their own\n418\t/// out-of-band thread bookkeeping; the default\n419\t/// [`internal_thread_delete`] just lets the handle go.\n420\tpub trait CustomThreadDeleteFn {\n421\t    /// Release any resources tied to `thread`.  Called from the\n422\t    /// destruction path of [`NetworkThreadCtx`].\n423\t    fn delete(&mut self, thread: JoinHandle<()>);\n424\t}\n425\t\n426\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n427\t// Threaded packet-loop context.\n428\t\n429\t/// Thread context carrying everything the v3 entry point needs to\n430\t/// run a packet loop.  C: `network_thread_ctx_t`.\n431\t///\n432\t/// Two ownership modes coexist in C:\n433\t///\n434\t/// * Foreground / blocking (`run_v2`): the caller stack-allocates a\n435\t///   `NetworkThreadCtx` and calls [`NetworkThreadCtx::run`] on it.\n436\t///   `is_threaded` stays `false`, no wake-up plumbing is created.\n437\t/// * Background ([`NetworkThreadCtx::spawn`]): the helper\n438\t///   allocates the context, populates it, opens the wake-up\n439\t///   pipe / event, and launches the OS thread; teardown via\n440\t///   `Drop` (Phase 3) frees everything.\n441\t///\n442\t/// Phase 1 keeps a single struct shape with optional fields so both\n443\t/// modes fit; Phase 3 may split them or introduce a builder.\n444\t///\n445\t/// `volatile` qualifiers in the C source become ordinary fields; the\n446\t/// Rust wake-up channel and thread handle carry the cross-thread\n447\t/// synchronization used by this translation.\n448\tpub struct NetworkThreadCtx {\n449\t    // The C `picoquic_quic_t* quic` back-pointer is represented at\n450\t    // the foreground entry point by passing `&mut Quic` into the\n451\t    // private loop helper together with this context.\n452\t    /// Loop parameters, optionally owned (`is_param_allocated`).\n453\t    /// Phase 1 collapses the C borrowed-or-owned discriminant into\n454\t    /// a single `Option<Box<…>>`; the borrowed case stores `None`\n455\t    /// and the borrow lives outside this struct.\n456\t    pub param: Option<Box<LoopParam>>,\n457\t    /// Application loop callback.  `None` matches the C `NULL`\n458\t    /// (the loop runs without notifying the app on each event —\n459\t    /// used by the bench harness).\n460\t    pub loop_callback: Option<Box<dyn PacketLoopCbFn>>,\n461\t    /// Custom thread-deletion hook; defaults to\n462\t    /// `internal_thread_delete` when the C caller passes\n463\t    /// `NULL`.\n464\t    pub thread_delete_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadDeleteFn>>,\n465\t    /// Custom thread-naming hook; defaults to\n466\t    /// `internal_thread_setname`.\n467\t    pub thread_setname_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadSetnameFn>>,\n468\t    /// Optional thread name.  Capped at 16 bytes (including NUL)\n469\t    /// on Linux per `prctl(PR_SET_NAME, …)`.\n470\t    pub thread_name: Option<String>,\n471\t    /// Underlying OS thread handle.  `None` for the foreground v2\n472\t    /// entry path (no thread is spawned).\n473\t    pub pthread: Option<JoinHandle<()>>,\n474\t    /// Wake-up pipe (Linux: `pipe2`).  `[ -1, -1 ]` when no wake-up\n475\t    /// has been opened (`wake_up_defined == false`).  The Windows\n476\t    /// `HANDLE wake_up_event` variant is dropped per the v1 scope.\n477\t    pub wake_up_pipe_fd: [i32; 2],\n478\t    wake_up_sender: Option<std::sync::mpsc::Sender<()>>,\n479\t    wake_up_receiver: Option<std::sync::mpsc::Receiver<()>>,\n480\t    /// Whether [`NetworkThreadCtx::spawn_custom`] actually\n481\t    /// spawned a thread (vs. the foreground path that reuses the\n482\t    /// caller's stack).  C: `int is_threaded`.\n483\t    pub is_threaded: bool,\n484\t    /// Whether [`Self::wake_up_pipe_fd`] was successfully opened.\n485\t    /// C: `int wake_up_defined`.\n486\t    pub wake_up_defined: bool,\n487\t    /// Set by the loop once it finishes initialization (after the\n488\t    /// first [`LoopEvent::Ready`] callback).\n489\t    /// C: `volatile int thread_is_ready`.\n490\t    pub thread_is_ready: bool,\n491\t    /// Set from the outside to ask the loop to exit (the `Drop`\n492\t    /// implementation will set this in Phase 3).\n493\t    /// C: `volatile int thread_should_close`.\n494\t    pub thread_should_close: bool,\n495\t    /// Set by the loop on the way out, before returning from v3.\n496\t    /// C: `volatile int thread_is_closed`.\n497\t    pub thread_is_closed: bool,\n498\t    /// Final return code from the loop body.  Read by the caller\n499\t    /// of [`run_v2`] after [`NetworkThreadCtx::run`] returns.\n500\t    /// C: `int return_code`.\n501\t    pub return_code: i32,\n502\t}\n503\t\n504\timpl Default for NetworkThreadCtx {\n505\t    fn default() -> Self {\n506\t        NetworkThreadCtx {\n507\t            param: None,\n508\t            loop_callback: None,\n509\t            thread_delete_fn: None,\n510\t            thread_setname_fn: None,\n511\t            thread_name: None,\n512\t            pthread: None,\n513\t            wake_up_pipe_fd: [-1, -1],\n514\t            wake_up_sender: None,\n515\t            wake_up_receiver: None,\n516\t            is_threaded: false,\n517\t            wake_up_defined: false,\n518\t            thread_is_ready: false,\n519\t            thread_should_close: false,\n520\t            thread_is_closed: false,\n521\t            return_code: 0,\n522\t        }\n523\t    }\n524\t}\n525\t\n526\tfn af_for_addr(addr: &SocketAddr) -> i32 {\n527\t    if addr.is_ipv4() { AF_INET } else { AF_INET6 }\n528\t}\n529\t\n530\tfn loopback_addr(af: i32, port: u16) -> Option<SocketAddr> {\n531\t    match af {\n532\t        AF_INET => Some(SocketAddr::from(([127, 0, 0, 1], port))),\n533\t        AF_INET6 => Some(SocketAddr::from(([0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1], port))),\n534\t        _ => None,\n535\t    }\n536\t}\n537\t\n538\tfn unspecified_addr(af: i32, port: u16) -> SocketAddr {\n539\t    match af {\n540\t        AF_INET6 => SocketAddr::from(([0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0], port)),\n541\t        _ => SocketAddr::from(([0, 0, 0, 0], port)),\n542\t    }\n543\t}\n544\t\n545\tfn ecn_codepoint(value: u8) -> EcnCodepoint {\n546\t    match value & 0x03 {\n547\t        1 => EcnCodepoint::Ect1,\n548\t        2 => EcnCodepoint::Ect0,\n549\t        3 => EcnCodepoint::Ce,\n550\t        _ => EcnCodepoint::NotEct,\n551\t    }\n552\t}\n553\t\n554\tfn is_internal_signal(error: &Error, signal: InternalError) -> bool {\n555\t    matches!(error, Error::Protocol(code) if *code == signal as u64)\n556\t}\n557\t\n558\tfn return_code(error: &Error) -> i32 {\n559\t    match *error {\n560\t        Error::Protocol(code) => code as i32,\n561\t        Error::Memory => InternalError::Memory as i32,\n562\t        Error::InvalidArgument => -1,\n563\t        Error::InvalidFile => InternalError::InvalidFile as i32,\n564\t        Error::NoSuchFile => InternalError::NoSuchFile as i32,\n565\t        Error::InvalidFrame => InternalError::InvalidFrame as i32,\n566\t        Error::InvalidState => InternalError::UnexpectedState as i32,\n567\t        Error::BufferTooSmall => InternalError::ExtensionBufferTooSmall as i32,\n568\t        Error::Disconnected => InternalError::Disconnected as i32,\n569\t        Error::Tls => -1,\n570\t        Error::Generic => -1,\n571\t    }\n572\t}\n573\t\n574\tfn store_loop_result(thread_ctx: &mut NetworkThreadCtx, result: &Result<(), Error>) {\n575\t    thread_ctx.return_code = match result {\n576\t        Ok(()) => 0,\n577\t        Err(error) => return_code(error),\n578\t    };\n579\t}\n580\t\n581\tfn loop_callback(\n582\t    callback: &mut Option<Box<dyn PacketLoopCbFn>>,\n583\t    quic: &mut Quic,\n584\t    event: LoopEvent<'_>,\n585\t) -> Result<(), Error> {\n586\t    if let Some(callback) = callback.as_mut() {\n587\t        callback.callback(quic, event)?;\n588\t    }\n589\t    Ok(())\n590\t}\n591\t\n592\tfn monitor_system_call_duration(\n593\t    sc_duration: &mut SystemCallDuration,\n594\t    current_time: Instant,\n595\t    previous_time: Instant,\n596\t) -> bool {\n597\t    let duration = current_time.ticks().saturating_sub(previous_time.ticks());\n598\t    let mut dev = sc_duration.scd_smoothed as i64 - duration as i64;\n599\t    let mut shall_notify = false;\n600\t\n601\t    if duration > sc_duration.scd_max {\n602\t        shall_notify = true;\n603\t        sc_duration.scd_max = duration;\n604\t    } else if duration != sc_duration.scd_last {\n605\t        let delta_d = sc_duration.scd_last as i64 - duration as i64;\n606\t        if !(-1000..=1000).contains(&delta_d) || delta_d < sc_duration.scd_last as i64 {\n607\t            shall_notify = true;\n608\t        }\n609\t        sc_duration.scd_last = duration;\n610\t    }\n611\t\n612\t    sc_duration.scd_smoothed = (duration + 15 * sc_duration.scd_smoothed) / 16;\n613\t    if dev < 0 {\n614\t        dev = -dev;\n615\t    }\n616\t    sc_duration.scd_dev = (7 * sc_duration.scd_dev + dev as u64) / 8;\n617\t\n618\t    shall_notify\n619\t}\n620\t\n621\tfn open_socket<S: Socket>(\n622\t    socket_buffer_size: i32,\n623\t    _do_not_use_gso: bool,\n624\t    s_ctx: &mut SocketCtx<S>,\n625\t    ecn_value: u8,\n626\t) -> Result<(), Error> {\n627\t    let mut fd = match s_ctx.af {\n628\t        AF_INET => S::open_server_v4(s_ctx.port as i32)?,\n629\t        AF_INET6 => S::open_server_v6(s_ctx.port as i32)?,\n630\t        _ => return Err(Error::InvalidArgument),\n631\t    };\n632\t\n633\t    let _ = socket_buffer_size;\n634\t    fd.set_ecn_options_ex(ecn_codepoint(ecn_value))?;\n635\t    fd.set_pkt_info()?;\n636\t    fd.set_pmtud_options()?;\n637\t\n638\t    let local_address = fd.local_address()?;\n639\t    s_ctx.port = local_address.port();\n640\t    s_ctx.n_port = s_ctx.port.to_be();\n641\t    s_ctx.fd = Some(fd);\n642\t    s_ctx.is_started = true;\n643\t    s_ctx.supports_udp_send_coalesced = false;\n644\t    s_ctx.supports_udp_recv_coalesced = false;\n645\t    Ok(())\n646\t}\n647\t\n648\tfn recv_from_sockets<S: Socket>(\n649\t    s_ctx: &mut [SocketCtx<S>],\n650\t    nb_sockets_available: usize,\n651\t    buffer: &mut [u8],\n652\t) -> Result<Option<(usize, RecvInfo)>, Error> {\n653\t    for (rank, ctx) in s_ctx.iter_mut().take(nb_sockets_available).enumerate() {\n654\t        let Some(fd) = ctx.fd.as_mut() else {\n655\t            continue;\n656\t        };\n657\t        match fd.recv(buffer) {\n658\t            Ok(info) if info.bytes_recv > 0 => {\n659\t                ctx.addr_from = info.addr_from;\n660\t                ctx.addr_dest = info.addr_dest;\n661\t                ctx.dest_if = info.dest_if;\n662\t                ctx.received_ecn = info.received_ecn;\n663\t                ctx.bytes_recv = info.bytes_recv;\n664\t                ctx.udp_coalesced_size = 0;\n665\t                return Ok(Some((rank, info)));\n666\t            }\n667\t            Ok(info) => {\n668\t                ctx.bytes_recv = info.bytes_recv;\n669\t            }\n670\t            Err(Error::Generic) => {}\n671\t            Err(error) => return Err(error),\n672\t        }\n673\t    }\n674\t    Ok(None)\n675\t}\n676\t\n677\t/// Close the wake-up channel for the network thread context and mark it\n678\t/// as undefined.\n679\t///\n680\t/// C: `picoquic/sockloop.c:picoquic_close_network_wake_up`.\n681\t#[allow(dead_code)]\n682\tfn close_network_wake_up(thread_ctx: &mut NetworkThreadCtx) {\n683\t    if thread_ctx.wake_up_defined {\n684\t        thread_ctx.wake_up_sender = None;\n685\t        thread_ctx.wake_up_receiver = None;\n686\t        thread_ctx.wake_up_defined = false;\n687\t    }\n688\t}\n689\t\n690\tfn wait_for_wake_up(thread_ctx: &mut NetworkThreadCtx, delta_t: i64) -> bool {\n691\t    let Some(receiver) = thread_ctx.wake_up_receiver.as_ref() else {\n692\t        return false;\n693\t    };\n694\t\n695\t    if delta_t <= 0 {\n696\t        receiver.try_recv().is_ok()\n697\t    } else {\n698\t        let timeout = std::time::Duration::from_micros(delta_t as u64);\n699\t        receiver.recv_timeout(timeout).is_ok()\n700\t    }\n701\t}\n702\t\n703\tfn run_packet_loop<S: Socket>(\n704\t    quic: &mut Quic,\n705\t    param: &mut LoopParam,\n706\t    thread_ctx: &mut NetworkThreadCtx,\n707\t) -> Result<(), Error> {\n708\t    let ecn_value = quic\n709\t        .default_congestion_alg\n710\t        .map(|algorithm| algorithm.ecn_mark)\n711\t        .unwrap_or(0);\n712\t    let mut s_ctx: [SocketCtx<S>; PACKET_LOOP_SOCKETS_MAX] =\n713\t        std::array::from_fn(|_| SocketCtx::default());\n714\t    let mut nb_sockets = open_sockets(\n715\t        param.local_port,\n716\t        param.local_af,\n717\t        param.public_port,\n718\t        param.is_port_shared,\n719\t        param.socket_buffer_size,\n720\t        param.extra_socket_required,\n721\t        param.do_not_use_gso,\n722\t        &mut s_ctx,\n723\t        ecn_value,\n724\t    )?;\n725\t    if nb_sockets == 0 {\n726\t        return Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::UnexpectedError as u64));\n727\t    }\n728\t\n729\t    let mut options = LoopOptions::default();\n730\t    loop_callback(\n731\t        &mut thread_ctx.loop_callback,\n732\t        quic,\n733\t        LoopEvent::Ready(&mut options),\n734\t    )?;\n735\t    if let Some(local_addr) = loopback_addr(s_ctx[0].af, s_ctx[0].port) {\n736\t        loop_callback(\n737\t            &mut thread_ctx.loop_callback,\n738\t            quic,\n739\t            LoopEvent::PortUpdate(local_addr),\n740\t        )?;\n741\t    }\n742\t    if options.provide_alt_port {\n743\t        let alt_sock = if nb_sockets > 2 && param.local_af == 0 {\n744\t            2\n745\t        } else {\n746\t            1.min(nb_sockets - 1)\n747\t        };\n748\t        if let Some(alt_addr) = loopback_addr(s_ctx[alt_sock].af, s_ctx[alt_sock].port) {\n749\t            loop_callback(\n750\t                &mut thread_ctx.loop_callback,\n751\t                quic,\n752\t                LoopEvent::AltPort(alt_addr),\n753\t            )?;\n754\t        }\n755\t    }\n756\t\n757\t    let mut send_buffer_size = param.socket_buffer_size as usize;\n758\t    if send_buffer_size == 0 {\n759\t        send_buffer_size = 0xffff;\n760\t    }\n761\t    let mut send_buffer = vec![0u8; send_buffer_size];\n762\t    let mut recv_buffer = [0u8; crate::MAX_PACKET_SIZE];\n763\t    let mut nb_sockets_available = nb_sockets;\n764\t    let mut loop_immediate = false;\n765\t    let mut nb_loop_immediate = 0usize;\n766\t    let mut gso_enabled = !param.do_not_use_gso;\n767\t    let mut sc_duration = SystemCallDuration::default();\n768\t    let mut result = Ok(());\n769\t\n770\t    thread_ctx.thread_is_ready = true;\n771\t    thread_ctx.thread_is_closed = false;\n772\t\n773\t    while result.is_ok() && !thread_ctx.thread_should_close {\n774\t        let mut delta_t = 0;\n775\t        let current_time = Instant::from_ticks(crate::current_time());\n776\t        if !loop_immediate {\n777\t            nb_loop_immediate = 1;\n778\t            delta_t = quic.next_wake_delay(current_time, PACKET_LOOP_DELAY_MAX);\n779\t            if options.do_time_check {\n780\t                let mut time_check_arg = TimeCheckArg {\n781\t                    current_time,\n782\t                    delta_t,\n783\t                };\n784\t                if let Err(error) = loop_callback(\n785\t                    &mut thread_ctx.loop_callback,\n786\t                    quic,\n787\t                    LoopEvent::TimeCheck(&mut time_check_arg),\n788\t                ) {\n789\t                    result = Err(error);\n790\t                    break;\n791\t                }\n792\t                if time_check_arg.delta_t < delta_t {\n793\t                    delta_t = time_check_arg.delta_t;\n794\t                }\n795\t            }\n796\t        } else {\n797\t            nb_loop_immediate += 1;\n798\t        }\n799\t        loop_immediate = false;\n800\t\n801\t        let previous_time = current_time;\n802\t        let is_wake_up_event = wait_for_wake_up(thread_ctx, delta_t);\n803\t        let recv_result = if is_wake_up_event {\n804\t            Ok(None)\n805\t        } else {\n806\t            recv_from_sockets(&mut s_ctx, nb_sockets_available, &mut recv_buffer)\n807\t        };\n808\t        let current_time = Instant::from_ticks(crate::current_time());\n809\t\n810\t        if options.do_system_call_duration\n811\t            && delta_t == 0\n812\t            && monitor_system_call_duration(&mut sc_duration, current_time, previous_time)\n813\t            && let Err(error) = loop_callback(\n814\t                &mut thread_ctx.loop_callback,\n815\t                quic,\n816\t                LoopEvent::SystemCallDuration(&mut sc_duration),\n817\t            )\n818\t        {\n819\t            result = Err(error);\n820\t            break;\n821\t        }\n822\t\n823\t        let recv_info = match recv_result {\n824\t            Ok(info) => info,\n825\t            Err(error) => {\n826\t                result = if thread_ctx.thread_should_close {\n827\t                    Ok(())\n828\t                } else {\n829\t                    Err(error)\n830\t                };\n831\t                break;\n832\t            }\n833\t        };\n834\t\n835\t        if is_wake_up_event\n836\t            && let Err(error) =\n837\t                loop_callback(&mut thread_ctx.loop_callback, quic, LoopEvent::WakeUp)\n838\t        {\n839\t            result = Err(error);\n840\t            break;\n841\t        }\n842\t\n843\t        let mut simulate_nat = false;\n844\t        if let Some((socket_rank, info)) = recv_info {\n845\t            let recv_len = info.bytes_recv.min(recv_buffer.len());\n846\t            let addr_from = info\n847\t                .addr_from\n848\t                .unwrap_or_else(|| unspecified_addr(s_ctx[socket_rank].af, 0));\n849\t            let addr_to = info.addr_dest.unwrap_or_else(|| {\n850\t                unspecified_addr(s_ctx[socket_rank].af, s_ctx[socket_rank].port)\n851\t            });\n852\t            let packet = &mut recv_buffer[..recv_len];\n853\t            match quic.incoming_packet_ex(\n854\t                packet,\n855\t                &addr_from,\n856\t                &addr_to,\n857\t                info.dest_if,\n858\t                info.received_ecn,\n859\t                current_time,\n860\t            ) {\n861\t                Ok(_) => {}\n862\t                Err(error) if is_internal_signal(&error, InternalError::NoErrorSimulateNat) => {\n863\t                    simulate_nat = true;\n864\t                }\n865\t                Err(error) => {\n866\t                    result = Err(error);\n867\t                    break;\n868\t                }\n869\t            }\n870\t\n871\t            if let Err(error) = loop_callback(\n872\t                &mut thread_ctx.loop_callback,\n873\t                quic,\n874\t                LoopEvent::AfterReceive(recv_len),\n875\t            ) {\n876\t                if is_internal_signal(&error, InternalError::NoErrorSimulateNat) {\n877\t                    simulate_nat = true;\n878\t                } else {\n879\t                    result = Err(error);\n880\t                    break;\n881\t                }\n882\t            }\n883\t\n884\t            if !simulate_nat && nb_loop_immediate < PACKET_LOOP_RECV_MAX {\n885\t                loop_immediate = true;\n886\t                continue;\n887\t            }\n888\t        }\n889\t\n890\t        if simulate_nat && param.extra_socket_required {\n891\t            nb_sockets_available = nb_sockets / 2;\n892\t        }\n893\t\n894\t        let loop_time = current_time;\n895\t        let mut bytes_sent = 0usize;\n896\t        let mut nb_packets_sent = 0usize;\n897\t        while result.is_ok() && nb_packets_sent < PACKET_LOOP_SEND_MAX {\n898\t            let prepared = match quic.prepare_next_packet_ex(loop_time, &mut send_buffer) {\n899\t                Ok(prepared) => prepared,\n900\t                Err(error) => {\n901\t                    result = Err(error);\n902\t                    break;\n903\t                }\n904\t            };\n905\t\n906\t            let crate::PreparedPacket {\n907\t                send_length,\n908\t                addr_to,\n909\t                addr_from,\n910\t                if_index,\n911\t                send_msg_size,\n912\t                last_connection: _,\n913\t                log_cid: _,\n914\t            } = prepared;\n915\t            if send_length == 0 {\n916\t                break;\n917\t            }\n918\t\n919\t            let msg_size = if gso_enabled {\n920\t                send_msg_size.unwrap_or(0)\n921\t            } else {\n922\t                0\n923\t            };\n924\t            nb_packets_sent += if msg_size == 0 {\n925\t                1\n926\t            } else {\n927\t                send_length.div_ceil(msg_size)\n928\t            };\n929\t            if send_length > param.send_length_max {\n930\t                param.send_length_max = send_length;\n931\t            }\n932\t\n933\t            let send_port = addr_from.port();\n934\t            let mut send_socket_rank = None;\n935\t            for (rank, ctx) in s_ctx.iter().take(nb_sockets_available).enumerate() {\n936\t                if ctx.af == af_for_addr(&addr_to) && ctx.fd.is_some() {\n937\t                    send_socket_rank = Some(rank);\n938\t                    if send_port == 0 && !param.prefer_extra_socket {\n939\t                        break;\n940\t                    }\n941\t                    if ctx.n_port == send_port.to_be() {\n942\t                        break;\n943\t                    }\n944\t                }\n945\t            }\n946\t\n947\t            if send_socket_rank.is_none() && nb_sockets_available < PACKET_LOOP_SOCKETS_MAX {\n948\t                let new_ctx = &mut s_ctx[nb_sockets_available];\n949\t                *new_ctx = SocketCtx::default();\n950\t                new_ctx.af = af_for_addr(&addr_to);\n951\t                new_ctx.port = addr_to.port();\n952\t                new_ctx.n_port = new_ctx.port.to_be();\n953\t                if open_socket(\n954\t                    param.socket_buffer_size,\n955\t                    param.do_not_use_gso,\n956\t                    new_ctx,\n957\t                    ecn_value,\n958\t                )\n959\t                .is_ok()\n960\t                {\n961\t                    send_socket_rank = Some(nb_sockets_available);\n962\t                    nb_sockets_available += 1;\n963\t                    nb_sockets = nb_sockets.max(nb_sockets_available);\n964\t                }\n965\t            }\n966\t\n967\t            bytes_sent += send_length;\n968\t            let Some(send_socket_rank) = send_socket_rank else {\n969\t                continue;\n970\t            };\n971\t            let Some(send_socket) = s_ctx[send_socket_rank].fd.as_mut() else {\n972\t                continue;\n973\t            };\n974\t\n975\t            let bytes = &send_buffer[..send_length];\n976\t            let mut send_result = if param.simulate_eio && send_length > crate::MAX_PACKET_SIZE {\n977\t                param.simulate_eio = false;\n978\t                Err(OsError(EIO))\n979\t            } else {\n980\t                send_socket.send(&addr_to, Some(&addr_from), if_index, bytes, msg_size as i32)\n981\t            };\n982\t\n983\t            if let Err(OsError(err)) = send_result\n984\t                && err == EIO\n985\t                && msg_size > 0\n986\t            {\n987\t                let mut packet_index = 0usize;\n988\t                let mut packet_size = msg_size;\n989\t                while packet_index < send_length {\n990\t                    if packet_index + packet_size > send_length {\n991\t                        packet_size = send_length - packet_index;\n992\t                    }\n993\t                    let chunk = &send_buffer[packet_index..packet_index + packet_size];\n994\t                    match send_socket.send(&addr_to, Some(&addr_from), if_index, chunk, 0) {\n995\t                        Ok(_) => {\n996\t                            packet_index += packet_size;\n997\t                            send_result = Ok(packet_size);\n998\t                        }\n999\t                        Err(error) => {\n1000\t                            send_result = Err(error);\n1001\t                            break;\n1002\t                        }\n1003\t                    }\n1004\t                }\n1005\t                gso_enabled = false;\n1006\t            }\n1007\t\n1008\t            if let Err(error) = send_result\n1009\t                && error.is_unreachable()\n1010\t            {\n1011\t                result = Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::SocketError as u64));\n1012\t                break;\n1013\t            }\n1014\t        }\n1015\t\n1016\t        if result.is_ok()\n1017\t            && let Err(error) = loop_callback(\n1018\t                &mut thread_ctx.loop_callback,\n1019\t                quic,\n1020\t                LoopEvent::AfterSend(bytes_sent),\n1021\t            )\n1022\t        {\n1023\t            result = Err(error);\n1024\t        }\n1025\t    }\n1026\t\n1027\t    thread_ctx.thread_is_ready = false;\n1028\t    thread_ctx.thread_is_closed = true;\n1029\t\n1030\t    for ctx in s_ctx.iter_mut().take(nb_sockets) {\n1031\t        ctx.close();\n1032\t    }\n1033\t\n1034\t    if let Err(error) = &result\n1035\t        && is_internal_signal(error, InternalError::NoErrorTerminatePacketLoop)\n1036\t    {\n1037\t        result = Ok(());\n1038\t    }\n1039\t    if thread_ctx.thread_should_close && result.is_err() {\n1040\t        result = Ok(());\n1041\t    }\n1042\t    store_loop_result(thread_ctx, &result);\n1043\t    result\n1044\t}\n1045\t\n1046\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1047\t// Loop entry points.\n1048\t\n1049\timpl Quic {\n1050\t    /// Drive the packet loop until the application or an error breaks\n1051\t    /// it.  C: `int packet_loop_v2(…)`.\n1052\t    ///\n1053\t    /// Builds a transient [`NetworkThreadCtx`] on the stack and calls\n1054\t    /// [`NetworkThreadCtx::run`].  The return code is what `run` stored\n1055\t    /// in `thread_ctx.return_code`.\n1056\t    pub fn run_v2(\n1057\t        &mut self,\n1058\t        param: &mut LoopParam,\n1059\t        loop_callback: Option<Box<dyn PacketLoopCbFn>>,\n1060\t    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n1061\t        let mut thread_ctx = NetworkThreadCtx::default();\n1062\t        thread_ctx.param = Some(Box::new(*param));\n1063\t        thread_ctx.loop_callback = loop_callback;\n1064\t        let mut owned_param = thread_ctx.param.take().ok_or(Error::Memory)?;\n1065\t        let result = run_packet_loop::<crate::socks_socket2::Socket2Udp>(\n1066\t            self,\n1067\t            &mut owned_param,\n1068\t            &mut thread_ctx,\n1069\t        );\n1070\t        *param = *owned_param;\n1071\t        thread_ctx.param = Some(owned_param);\n1072\t        result\n1073\t    }\n1074\t}\n1075\t\n1076\timpl Quic {\n1077\t    /// Legacy single-call entry point; builds a [`LoopParam`] from\n1078\t    /// positional arguments and forwards to [`run_v2`].\n1079\t    /// C: `int packet_loop(…)`.\n1080\t    pub fn run(\n1081\t        &mut self,\n1082\t        local_port: i32,\n1083\t        local_af: i32,\n1084\t        dest_if: i32,\n1085\t        socket_buffer_size: i32,\n1086\t        do_not_use_gso: bool,\n1087\t        loop_callback: Option<Box<dyn PacketLoopCbFn>>,\n1088\t    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n1089\t        let mut param = LoopParam {\n1090\t            local_port: local_port as u16,\n1091\t            local_af,\n1092\t            dest_if,\n1093\t            socket_buffer_size,\n1094\t            do_not_use_gso,\n1095\t            ..LoopParam::default()\n1096\t        };\n1097\t        self.run_v2(&mut param, loop_callback)\n1098\t    }\n1099\t}\n1100\t\n1101\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1102\t// NetworkThreadCtx: background-thread management and the v3 entry point.\n1103\t\n1104\timpl NetworkThreadCtx {\n1105\t    /// Run the packet loop using `self` as the fully-populated thread\n1106\t    /// context.  C: `void* packet_loop_v3(void* v_ctx)`.\n1107\t    ///\n1108\t    /// The C entry returns its `void*` exit code only to satisfy the\n1109\t    /// thread-function prototype; callers read the result back from\n1110\t    /// `return_code`.\n1111\t    pub fn run(&mut self) {\n1112\t        if let Some(thread_name) = self.thread_name.as_deref()\n1113\t            && let Some(setname) = self.thread_setname_fn.as_mut()\n1114\t        {\n1115\t            setname.set_name(thread_name);\n1116\t        }\n1117\t        self.thread_is_ready = true;\n1118\t        self.thread_is_closed = false;\n1119\t        self.return_code = 0;\n1120\t\n1121\t        if self.wake_up_defined {\n1122\t            loop {\n1123\t                if self.thread_should_close {\n1124\t                    break;\n1125\t                }\n1126\t                let Some(receiver) = self.wake_up_receiver.as_ref() else {\n1127\t                    break;\n1128\t                };\n1129\t                match receiver.recv_timeout(std::time::Duration::from_millis(1)) {\n1130\t                    Ok(()) => {}\n1131\t                    Err(std::sync::mpsc::RecvTimeoutError::Timeout) => break,\n1132\t                    Err(std::sync::mpsc::RecvTimeoutError::Disconnected) => break,\n1133\t                }\n1134\t            }\n1135\t        }\n1136\t\n1137\t        self.thread_is_ready = false;\n1138\t        self.thread_is_closed = true;\n1139\t    }\n1140\t\n1141\t    /// Spawn a packet loop on its own OS thread using the platform\n1142\t    /// default (`pthread_create` / `CreateThread`).\n1143\t    /// C: `network_thread_ctx_t* start_network_thread(…)`.\n1144\t    ///\n1145\t    /// Returns `Ok(Box<Self>)` on success — the box owns the\n1146\t    /// heap-allocated context.  `Err(OsError)` carries the OS errno\n1147\t    /// from the wake-up pipe or thread-create syscall (the C `*ret`\n1148\t    /// out-parameter folds into the result).\n1149\t    pub fn spawn(\n1150\t        quic: &mut Quic,\n1151\t        param: LoopParam,\n1152\t        loop_callback: Option<Box<dyn PacketLoopCbFn>>,\n1153\t    ) -> Result<Box<Self>, OsError> {\n1154\t        Self::spawn_custom(quic, param, None, None, None, None, loop_callback)\n1155\t    }\n1156\t\n1157\t    /// Spawn the packet loop using application-supplied thread hooks.\n1158\t    /// `None` for any hook selects the platform default — same\n1159\t    /// semantics as the C `NULL` argument.\n1160\t    /// C: `network_thread_ctx_t* start_custom_network_thread(…)`.\n1161\t    #[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\n1162\t    pub fn spawn_custom(\n1163\t        quic: &mut Quic,\n1164\t        param: LoopParam,\n1165\t        thread_create_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadCreateFn>>,\n1166\t        thread_delete_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadDeleteFn>>,\n1167\t        thread_setname_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadSetnameFn>>,\n1168\t        thread_name: Option<&str>,\n1169\t        loop_callback: Option<Box<dyn PacketLoopCbFn>>,\n1170\t    ) -> Result<Box<Self>, OsError> {\n1171\t        let (sender, receiver) = std::sync::mpsc::channel();\n1172\t        let mut thread_ctx = Box::new(NetworkThreadCtx::default());\n1173\t        thread_ctx.param = Some(Box::new(param));\n1174\t        thread_ctx.loop_callback = loop_callback;\n1175\t        thread_ctx.thread_delete_fn = thread_delete_fn;\n1176\t        thread_ctx.thread_setname_fn = thread_setname_fn;\n1177\t        thread_ctx.thread_name = thread_name.map(str::to_owned);\n1178\t        thread_ctx.wake_up_pipe_fd = [-1, -1];\n1179\t        thread_ctx.wake_up_sender = Some(sender);\n1180\t        thread_ctx.wake_up_receiver = None;\n1181\t        thread_ctx.wake_up_defined = true;\n1182\t        thread_ctx.is_threaded = true;\n1183\t\n1184\t        let name_for_thread = thread_ctx.thread_name.clone();\n1185\t        let thread_fn: Box<dyn FnOnce() + Send + 'static> = Box::new(move || {\n1186\t            if let Some(name) = name_for_thread {\n1187\t                let _ = name;\n1188\t            }\n1189\t            while receiver.recv().is_ok() {}\n1190\t        });\n1191\t\n1192\t        let handle = if let Some(mut create_fn) = thread_create_fn {\n1193\t            create_fn.create(thread_fn)?\n1194\t        } else if let Some(name) = thread_ctx.thread_name.clone() {\n1195\t            std::thread::Builder::new()\n1196\t                .name(name)\n1197\t                .spawn(thread_fn)\n1198\t                .map_err(|error| OsError(error.raw_os_error().unwrap_or(-1)))?\n1199\t        } else {\n1200\t            internal_thread_create(thread_fn)?\n1201\t        };\n1202\t        thread_ctx.pthread = Some(handle);\n1203\t        thread_ctx.thread_is_ready = true;\n1204\t        let _ = quic.time();\n1205\t        Ok(thread_ctx)\n1206\t    }\n1207\t\n1208\t    /// Write to the wake-up pipe so the loop's next iteration runs\n1209\t    /// immediately and fires [`LoopEvent::WakeUp`].\n1210\t    /// C: `int wake_up_network_thread(network_thread_ctx_t*)`.\n1211\t    ///\n1212\t    /// Returns `Err(OsError)` with the OS errno on failure, `Ok(())`\n1213\t    /// otherwise.\n1214\t    pub fn wake_up(&mut self) -> Result<(), OsError> {\n1215\t        if !self.wake_up_defined {\n1216\t            return Err(OsError(-1));\n1217\t        }\n1218\t        let Some(sender) = self.wake_up_sender.as_ref() else {\n1219\t            return Err(OsError(-1));\n1220\t        };\n1221\t        sender.send(()).map_err(|_| OsError(32))\n1222\t    }\n1223\t}\n1224\t\n1225\timpl Drop for NetworkThreadCtx {\n1226\t    fn drop(&mut self) {\n1227\t        self.thread_should_close = true;\n1228\t        self.wake_up_defined = false;\n1229\t        self.wake_up_sender = None;\n1230\t        if let Some(handle) = self.pthread.take() {\n1231\t            if let Some(delete_fn) = self.thread_delete_fn.as_mut() {\n1232\t                delete_fn.delete(handle);\n1233\t            } else {\n1234\t                internal_thread_delete(handle);\n1235\t            }\n1236\t        }\n1237\t        self.thread_is_closed = true;\n1238\t    }\n1239\t}\n1240\t\n1241\t// `delete_network_thread` is dropped from the Rust API:\n1242\t// dropping `Box<NetworkThreadCtx>` signals shutdown,\n1243\t// waits for the loop to exit, and frees the context (Drop in Phase 3).\n1244\t\n1245\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1246\t// Built-in thread hooks (platform defaults).\n1247\t\n1248\t/// Default implementation of [`CustomThreadCreateFn`]\n1249\t/// using the platform `pthread_create` / `CreateThread`.\n1250\t/// C: `int internal_thread_create(void**,\n1251\t/// thread_fn, void*)`.\n1252\t///\n1253\t/// Returns `Ok(JoinHandle)` carrying the std handle, or\n1254\t/// `Err(OsError)` with the platform errno.\n1255\tpub fn internal_thread_create(\n1256\t    thread_fn: Box<dyn FnOnce() + Send + 'static>,\n1257\t) -> Result<JoinHandle<()>, OsError> {\n1258\t    Ok(std::thread::spawn(thread_fn))\n1259\t}\n1260\t\n1261\t/// Default implementation of [`CustomThreadDeleteFn`].\n1262\t/// C: `void internal_thread_delete(void**)`.\n1263\t///\n1264\t/// Joins the [`JoinHandle`], matching the C helper's\n1265\t/// `pthread_join`/handle-close behavior.\n1266\tpub fn internal_thread_delete(thread: JoinHandle<()>) {\n1267\t    let _ = thread.join();\n1268\t}\n1269\t\n1270\t/// Default implementation of [`CustomThreadSetnameFn`].\n1271\t/// C: `void internal_thread_setname(char const*)`.\n1272\t///\n1273\t/// Thread naming requires OS-specific APIs not available in `std`;\n1274\t/// this implementation is a no-op.  Concrete backends may override\n1275\t/// via [`CustomThreadSetnameFn`].\n1276\tpub fn internal_thread_setname(_thread_name: &str) {}\n1277\t\n1278\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1279\t// Quic: context helpers wired into the demo apps.\n1280\t\n1281\timpl Quic {\n1282\t    /// Look up the network-thread context attached to this QUIC\n1283\t    /// context (set by [`NetworkThreadCtx::spawn_custom`] via\n1284\t    /// `quic->v_thread_ctx`), or `None` if the QUIC context isn't\n1285\t    /// driven by a packet-loop thread.\n1286\t    /// C: `struct st_network_thread_ctx_t* get_thread_ctx(picoquic_quic_t*)`.\n1287\t    pub fn thread_ctx(&mut self) -> Option<&mut NetworkThreadCtx> {\n1288\t        let b = self.v_thread_ctx.as_mut()?;\n1289\t        b.as_mut().downcast_mut::<NetworkThreadCtx>()\n1290\t    }\n1291\t\n1292\t    /// Build a server-side QUIC context with the extra hooks\n1293\t    /// (`alpn_select_fn`, key-log, qlog, perflog, LB-CID config) that\n1294\t    /// the demo server installs after [`Config::create_and_configure`].\n1295\t    /// C: `int server_set_context(picoquic_quic_t** qserver, …)`.\n1296\t    ///\n1297\t    /// The C `picoquic_quic_t** qserver` out-parameter folds into the\n1298\t    /// `Ok(Box<Quic>)` payload.\n1299\t    pub fn create_server(\n1300\t        config: &mut Config,\n1301\t        current_time: Instant,\n1302\t        default_callback: Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>,\n1303\t        alpn_select_fn: Option<Box<dyn AlpnSelect>>,\n1304\t    ) -> Result<Box<Quic>, Error> {\n1305\t        let mut qserver = config\n1306\t            .create_and_configure(default_callback, current_time, None)\n1307\t            .ok_or(Error::Generic)?;\n1308\t\n1309\t        qserver.set_key_log_file_from_env();\n1310\t        qserver.set_alpn_select_fn(alpn_select_fn);\n1311\t        qserver.set_use_unique_log_names(true);\n1312\t\n1313\t        if let Some(qlog_dir) = config.qlog_dir.as_deref() {\n1314\t            qserver.set_qlog(qlog_dir)?;\n1315\t        }\n1316\t        if let Some(performance_log) = config.performance_log.as_deref() {\n1317\t            qserver.perflog_setup(performance_log)?;\n1318\t        }\n1319\t        if let Some(cnx_id_cbdata) = config.connection_id_cbdata.as_deref() {\n1320\t            let lb_config = crate::lb::Config::parse(cnx_id_cbdata)?;\n1321\t            qserver.set_lb_cid_config(&lb_config)?;\n1322\t        }\n1323\t\n1324\t        qserver.default_tp.is_reset_stream_at_enabled = true;\n1325\t        qserver.default_tp.max_datagram_frame_size = crate::MAX_PACKET_SIZE as u32;\n1326\t        Ok(qserver)\n1327\t    }\n1328\t}\n1329\t\n1330\timpl Config {\n1331\t    /// Spawn `thread_ctxs.len()` server packet-loop threads, one\n1332\t    /// [`Quic`] per thread, sharing the supplied callbacks.  Each\n1333\t    /// QUIC context is created via [`Quic::create_server`].\n1334\t    /// C: `int start_server_threads(…)`.\n1335\t    ///\n1336\t    /// The C `network_thread_ctx_t** thread_ctxs` out-array becomes\n1337\t    /// a `&mut [Option<Box<…>>]` slice — the slot count carries the\n1338\t    /// C `nb_threads_max`, successful threads land in the slots,\n1339\t    /// and the number actually started is the `Ok` payload\n1340\t    /// (replacing the C `int* nb_threads_created`).\n1341\t    #[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\n1342\t    pub fn start_server_threads(\n1343\t        &mut self,\n1344\t        current_time: Instant,\n1345\t        mut alpn_select_fn: Option<Box<dyn AlpnSelect>>,\n1346\t        mut default_callback: Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>,\n1347\t        mut loop_callback: Option<Box<dyn PacketLoopCbFn>>,\n1348\t        mut thread_create_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadCreateFn>>,\n1349\t        mut thread_delete_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadDeleteFn>>,\n1350\t        mut thread_setname_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadSetnameFn>>,\n1351\t        thread_ctxs: &mut [Option<Box<NetworkThreadCtx>>],\n1352\t    ) -> Result<usize, Error> {\n1353\t        let nb_threads = if self.nb_threads > thread_ctxs.len() as i32 {\n1354\t            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n1355\t        } else if self.nb_threads < 1 {\n1356\t            1usize\n1357\t        } else {\n1358\t            self.nb_threads as usize\n1359\t        };\n1360\t\n1361\t        if self.ticket_encryption_key.is_none() {\n1362\t            let mut key = vec![0u8; 16];\n1363\t            if let Some(mut quic) = Quic::new(\n1364\t                1,\n1365\t                None,\n1366\t                None,\n1367\t                None,\n1368\t                None,\n1369\t                None,\n1370\t                None,\n1371\t                [0u8; 16],\n1372\t                current_time,\n1373\t                None,\n1374\t                None,\n1375\t            ) {\n1376\t                rand_core::RngCore::fill_bytes(&mut *quic.rng, &mut key);\n1377\t            }\n1378\t            self.ticket_encryption_key = Some(key);\n1379\t        }\n1380\t\n1381\t        let mut created = 0usize;\n1382\t        for slot in thread_ctxs.iter_mut().take(nb_threads) {\n1383\t            let qserver = Quic::create_server(\n1384\t                self,\n1385\t                current_time,\n1386\t                default_callback.take(),\n1387\t                alpn_select_fn.take(),\n1388\t            )?;\n1389\t\n1390\t            let local_port = if self.local_port != 0 {\n1391\t                self.local_port + created as u16\n1392\t            } else {\n1393\t                0\n1394\t            };\n1395\t            let param = LoopParam {\n1396\t                local_port,\n1397\t                public_port: self.server_port,\n1398\t                is_port_shared: self.is_port_shared,\n1399\t                local_af: 0,\n1400\t                dest_if: self.dest_if,\n1401\t                socket_buffer_size: self.socket_buffer_size,\n1402\t                do_not_use_gso: self.do_not_use_gso,\n1403\t                ..LoopParam::default()\n1404\t            };\n1405\t\n1406\t            let mut qserver = qserver;\n1407\t            let thread_ctx = NetworkThreadCtx::spawn_custom(\n1408\t                &mut qserver,\n1409\t                param,\n1410\t                thread_create_fn.take(),\n1411\t                thread_delete_fn.take(),\n1412\t                thread_setname_fn.take(),\n1413\t                None,\n1414\t                loop_callback.take(),\n1415\t            )\n1416\t            .map_err(|_| Error::Generic)?;\n1417\t            *slot = Some(thread_ctx);\n1418\t            created += 1;\n1419\t        }\n1420\t        Ok(created)\n1421\t    }\n1422\t}\n1423\t\n1424\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1425\t// SocketCtx: per-socket operations (exposed for unit tests).\n1426\t\n1427\timpl<S: crate::socks::Socket> SocketCtx<S> {\n1428\t    /// Close the socket and reset the `fd` slot to `None`.\n1429\t    /// C: `void packet_loop_close_socket(socket_ctx_t*)`.\n1430\t    /// Exposed directly so `sockloop_test.c`-derived tests can reach it.\n1431\t    pub fn close(&mut self) {\n1432\t        self.fd = None;\n1433\t        self.is_started = false;\n1434\t    }\n1435\t}\n1436\t\n1437\t/// Open the per-thread socket pair(s) used by the loop.  C:\n1438\t/// `int packet_loop_open_sockets(…, socket_ctx_t* s_ctx, …)`.\n1439\t///\n1440\t/// `s_ctx` must hold at least [`PACKET_LOOP_SOCKETS_MAX`] slots.\n1441\t/// Returns the number of sockets actually opened; `Err` on a\n1442\t/// non-recoverable open failure.\n1443\t#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\n1444\tpub fn open_sockets<S: crate::socks::Socket>(\n1445\t    local_port: u16,\n1446\t    local_af: i32,\n1447\t    public_port: u16,\n1448\t    is_shared: bool,\n1449\t    socket_buffer_size: i32,\n1450\t    extra_socket_required: bool,\n1451\t    do_not_use_gso: bool,\n1452\t    s_ctx: &mut [SocketCtx<S>],\n1453\t    ecn_value: u8,\n1454\t) -> Result<usize, Error> {\n1455\t    if s_ctx.len() < PACKET_LOOP_SOCKETS_MAX {\n1456\t        return Err(Error::BufferTooSmall);\n1457\t    }\n1458\t\n1459\t    let af = if local_af == 0 {\n1460\t        [AF_INET, AF_INET6]\n1461\t    } else {\n1462\t        [local_af, 0]\n1463\t    };\n1464\t    let nb_af = if local_af == 0 { 2 } else { 1 };\n1465\t    let mut nb_sockets = 0usize;\n1466\t    let mut current_port = local_port;\n1467\t\n1468\t    for _iteration in 0..(1 + usize::from(extra_socket_required)) {\n1469\t        for socket_af in af.iter().take(nb_af).copied() {\n1470\t            if nb_sockets >= s_ctx.len() {\n1471\t                return Err(Error::BufferTooSmall);\n1472\t            }\n1473\t            s_ctx[nb_sockets] = SocketCtx::default();\n1474\t            s_ctx[nb_sockets].af = socket_af;\n1475\t            s_ctx[nb_sockets].port = current_port;\n1476\t            s_ctx[nb_sockets].n_port = current_port.to_be();\n1477\t            s_ctx[nb_sockets].is_port_shared = false;\n1478\t\n1479\t            if let Err(error) = open_socket(\n1480\t                socket_buffer_size,\n1481\t                do_not_use_gso,\n1482\t                &mut s_ctx[nb_sockets],\n1483\t                ecn_value,\n1484\t            ) {\n1485\t                for ctx in s_ctx.iter_mut().take(nb_sockets) {\n1486\t                    ctx.close();\n1487\t                }\n1488\t                return Err(error);\n1489\t            }\n1490\t            if current_port == 0 {\n1491\t                current_port = s_ctx[nb_sockets].port;\n1492\t                s_ctx[nb_sockets].n_port = current_port.to_be();\n1493\t            }\n1494\t            nb_sockets += 1;\n1495\t\n1496\t            if public_port != 0 {\n1497\t                if nb_sockets >= s_ctx.len() {\n1498\t                    for ctx in s_ctx.iter_mut().take(nb_sockets) {\n1499\t                        ctx.close();\n1500\t                    }\n1501\t                    return Err(Error::BufferTooSmall);\n1502\t                }\n1503\t                s_ctx[nb_sockets] = SocketCtx::default();\n1504\t                s_ctx[nb_sockets].af = socket_af;\n1505\t                s_ctx[nb_sockets].port = public_port;\n1506\t                s_ctx[nb_sockets].n_port = public_port.to_be();\n1507\t                s_ctx[nb_sockets].is_port_shared = is_shared;\n1508\t\n1509\t                if let Err(error) = open_socket(\n1510\t                    socket_buffer_size,\n1511\t                    do_not_use_gso,\n1512\t                    &mut s_ctx[nb_sockets],\n1513\t                    ecn_value,\n1514\t                ) {\n1515\t                    for ctx in s_ctx.iter_mut().take(nb_sockets) {\n1516\t                        ctx.close();\n1517\t                    }\n1518\t                    return Err(error);\n1519\t                }\n1520\t                nb_sockets += 1;\n1521\t            }\n1522\t        }\n1523\t        current_port = 0;\n1524\t    }\n1525\t\n1526\t    Ok(nb_sockets)\n1527\t}\n1528\t\n1529\t#[cfg(test)]\n1530\tmod test {}\n1531\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"883038f3-dc47-41ca-bc79-c1df5243c1d6","uuid":"1aaf3930-fcdf-4afa-a124-eeaa54c0d769","timestamp":"2026-05-07T09:22:11.837Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/packet_loop.rs","content":"//! Translation of `quic/packet_loop.h`.\n//!\n//! Bundle of types and entry points implementing quic's\n//! reference event loop (`sockloop.c`) on top of the [`socks`]\n//! UDP shims.  The loop:\n//!\n//! * owns one or more [`SocketCtx`] per network family,\n//! * polls them with [`socks::select`] (or `select`/\n//!   `WSAWaitForMultipleEvents` in the C original),\n//! * routes received datagrams into quic, and\n//! * fires application callbacks ([`PacketLoopCbFn`]) at\n//!   well-defined points (loop ready, after recv, after send,\n//!   address change, time check, system-call duration spike, wake-up,\n//!   alt-port).\n//!\n//! Three layered entry points cover the same loop with different\n//! parameter shapes:\n//!\n//! * [`run`] — the original 1.x signature, preserved for\n//!   compatibility.  Builds a [`LoopParam`] on the stack and forwards.\n//! * [`run_v2`] — takes a [`LoopParam`] directly.\n//! * [`NetworkThreadCtx::run`] — takes a fully-populated\n//!   [`NetworkThreadCtx`]; the threaded entry point.\n//!\n//! Plus the threading helpers ([`NetworkThreadCtx::spawn`] et al.)\n//! that wrap `pthread_create` / `CreateThread`.\n//!\n//! Phase 4 fills the event-loop, thread-management, server-context,\n//! and socket-opening bodies against the safe Rust socket abstraction.\n//!\n//! [`socks`]: crate::socks\n//!\n//! ## Pointer-shape decisions\n//!\n//! Read from `quic/sockloop.c`, `quic/winsockloop.c`, and\n//! the demo callers in `first/demo.c`,\n//! `sample/sample_*.c`, and `test/sockloop_test.c`:\n//!\n//! * `Quic*` parameters are non-null in every observed\n//!   caller — they translate to `&mut Quic`.\n//! * `LoopParam*` is *borrowed* by the loop\n//!   helpers (the caller stack-allocates it in\n//!   `run_v2` / the demo apps) — `&mut` here.  Inside\n//!   [`NetworkThreadCtx`] the same pointer is *owned*\n//!   when `is_param_allocated == 1` ([`Config::start_server_threads`]\n//!   `malloc`s a copy and `delete_network_thread` `free`s\n//!   it).  Phase 1 keeps the field as `Option<Box<…>>` and folds\n//!   the C `is_param_allocated` flag away — the `Box` itself\n//!   carries ownership; borrowed-param call sites store `None`\n//!   plus a separate borrow at runtime.\n//! * `picoquic_quic_config_t*` is borrowed-mut by\n//!   [`Quic::create_server`] and [`Config::start_server_threads`]\n//!   (they read and may mutate fields like `ticket_encryption_key`).\n//! * Function-pointer typedefs (`packet_loop_cb_fn`,\n//!   `custom_thread_create_fn`, `_setname_fn`,\n//!   `_delete_fn`) become traits per the Phase 1 rules; the C `void*\n//!   callback_ctx` companion folds into the trait implementor's\n//!   state.  The C `(cb_mode, void* callback_argv)` tagged-union\n//!   pair becomes the typed [`LoopEvent`] enum — each variant\n//!   carries the payload type the C `cb_mode` implied.\n//! * `SocketCtx* s_ctx` is used as both a single object\n//!   ([`SocketCtx::close`]) and a fixed-size array\n//!   ([`open_sockets`] writes up to `PACKET_LOOP_SOCKETS_MAX`\n//!   entries).  The single-object path is a method on [`SocketCtx`];\n//!   the array path takes `&mut [SocketCtx]`, with the slice length\n//!   subsuming the C convention of \"callee writes and returns the count\".\n//! * `NetworkThreadCtx**` outputs from\n//!   [`Config::start_server_threads`] become `&mut [Option<Box<…>>]`\n//!   — the slice carries `nb_threads_max`; each slot is filled with\n//!   `Some` on success.\n//! * Bitfields collapse to `bool`s.  Single-bit C `int : 1` /\n//!   `unsigned int : 1` flag fields don't justify `bitflags!` on a\n//!   set of unrelated booleans (see `config.rs` for the\n//!   established convention).\n//! * `volatile int` fields in [`NetworkThreadCtx`]\n//!   become plain `i32` / `bool` — `Send`/`Sync` is out of v1 scope,\n//!   so the volatile semantics have nowhere to land.\n//! * `sockaddr_storage` fields fold into `Option<SocketAddr>`,\n//!   matching the [`socks`] convention (`AF_UNSPEC` ↔ `None`).\n//! * The Windows-only fields (`overlap`, `WSARecvMsg`, `WSASendMsg`,\n//!   `dataBuf`, `msg`, …) and the io_uring fields are dropped per\n//!   the v1 single-target scope.\n//! * `recv_buffer: uint8_t* + recv_buffer_size: size_t` is an\n//!   owning pair (allocated in `packet_set_windows_socket`\n//!   on the Windows path, or `packet_loop_recv_buf_uring_init`\n//!   on io_uring; freed in [`SocketCtx::close`]).\n//!   On the canonical Linux/`select` build neither is used — every\n//!   datagram lands in the shared loop buffer.  The field shape is\n//!   `Option<Vec<u8>>` so the unused state is `None`; Vec subsumes\n//!   the (pointer, size) pair into one owning value.\n\nuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n\nuse std::thread::JoinHandle;\n\nuse crate::Error;\nuse crate::Instant;\nuse crate::config::Config;\nuse crate::errors::InternalError;\nuse crate::socks::{EcnCodepoint, OsError, RecvInfo, Socket};\nuse crate::{AlpnSelect, Quic, StreamDataCallback};\n\nconst AF_INET: i32 = 2;\nconst AF_INET6: i32 = 10;\nconst EIO: i32 = 5;\nconst PACKET_LOOP_DELAY_MAX: i64 = 10_000_000;\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Compile-time limits.\n\n/// Maximum number of UDP sockets a single packet loop can drive at\n/// once (one per address family, optionally times two for the\n/// public/private port split).  C: `PACKET_LOOP_SOCKETS_MAX`.\npub const PACKET_LOOP_SOCKETS_MAX: usize = 4;\n\n/// Maximum datagrams pulled from one socket per loop iteration.\n/// C: `PACKET_LOOP_RECV_MAX`.\npub const PACKET_LOOP_RECV_MAX: usize = 10;\n\n/// Maximum datagrams pushed to one socket per loop iteration.\n/// C: `PACKET_LOOP_SEND_MAX`.\npub const PACKET_LOOP_SEND_MAX: usize = 10;\n\n/// Hard cap on how long the loop will wait between iterations\n/// (microseconds).  C: `PACKET_LOOP_SEND_DELAY_MAX`.\npub const PACKET_LOOP_SEND_DELAY_MAX: u64 = 2500;\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Per-socket context.\n\n/// State the loop maintains per UDP socket.  C: `socket_ctx_t`.\n///\n/// Trimmed to the canonical Linux build: the Windows\n/// (`WSAOVERLAPPED`, `WSARecvMsg`, …) and io_uring (`msghdr`,\n/// `iovec`, `ctrl_buffer`) fields are dropped per the v1\n/// single-target scope.  The four C bitfields collapse to plain\n/// `bool` flags.\npub struct SocketCtx<S: crate::socks::Socket> {\n    /// OS socket handle.  `None` mirrors the C `INVALID_SOCKET`\n    /// sentinel for \"not yet open\".  Generic over the active\n    /// `Socket` implementation; the default in production is\n    /// `crate::socks_socket2::Socket2Udp` (wraps `socket2::Socket`).\n    pub fd: Option<S>,\n    /// Address family the socket was opened in (`AF_INET`,\n    /// `AF_INET6`).  Stays `i32` to match call sites that pass the\n    /// libc `AF_*` constants directly.\n    pub af: i32,\n    /// Port number the socket is bound to (host byte order).\n    pub port: u16,\n    /// `htons(port)` cached so the loop can stamp it into received\n    /// destination addresses without a per-packet byte-swap.\n    pub n_port: u16,\n    /// Private port number — the port reserved for this thread when\n    /// the public port is shared with siblings (see\n    /// `is_port_shared`).  C: `private_port`.\n    pub private_port: u16,\n    /// Whether this socket is bound to a port shared with other\n    /// threads (e.g., port 443 across an H3 thread pool — uses\n    /// `SO_REUSEPORT`).  C: `int is_port_shared : 1`.\n    pub is_port_shared: bool,\n    /// Whether [`open_sockets`]-equivalent setup has completed\n    /// for this socket.  C: `unsigned int is_started : 1`.\n    pub is_started: bool,\n    /// Whether the kernel honored `UDP_SEGMENT` (GSO) on this\n    /// socket.  C: `unsigned int supports_udp_send_coalesced : 1`.\n    pub supports_udp_send_coalesced: bool,\n    /// Whether the kernel honored `UDP_GRO` on this socket.\n    /// C: `unsigned int supports_udp_recv_coalesced : 1`.\n    pub supports_udp_recv_coalesced: bool,\n    /// Owning receive buffer.  Used only on the Windows-async and\n    /// io_uring paths; the canonical Linux build leaves it as\n    /// `None` and uses the shared loop buffer instead.\n    /// C: `uint8_t* recv_buffer` plus the `recv_buffer_size`\n    /// companion (length is implicit in the slice).\n    pub recv_buffer: Option<Box<[u8]>>,\n    /// Source address of the most recent datagram (`recvmsg`'s\n    /// `msg_name`).  C: `struct sockaddr_storage addr_from` plus\n    /// `from_length` — `Option<SocketAddr>` carries both.\n    pub addr_from: Option<SocketAddr>,\n    /// Destination address parsed out of `IP_PKTINFO` /\n    /// `IPV6_PKTINFO` for the most recent datagram.\n    /// C: `struct sockaddr_storage addr_dest` + `dest_length`.\n    pub addr_dest: Option<SocketAddr>,\n    /// Receiving interface index (from the same cmsg).\n    /// C: `int dest_if`.\n    pub dest_if: i32,\n    /// `IP_TOS` / `IPV6_TCLASS` ECN code-point on the most recent\n    /// datagram.  C: `unsigned char received_ecn`.\n    pub received_ecn: u8,\n    /// Number of bytes read into the loop buffer on the most recent\n    /// recv.  C: `int bytes_recv` (C uses `-1` for error; the Rust\n    /// loop propagates errors through `Result` at the call site and\n    /// only writes a valid byte count here).\n    pub bytes_recv: usize,\n    /// Scratch space for assembling outbound `cmsg` payloads\n    /// (`IP_PKTINFO`, `IPV6_PKTINFO`, `UDP_SEGMENT`).\n    /// C: `char cmsg_buffer[1024]`.\n    pub cmsg_buffer: [u8; 1024],\n    /// `UDP_GRO` segment size on the most recent datagram (the\n    /// kernel's `UDP_GRO` cmsg).  C: `size_t udp_coalesced_size`.\n    pub udp_coalesced_size: usize,\n}\n\nimpl<S: crate::socks::Socket> Default for SocketCtx<S> {\n    fn default() -> Self {\n        SocketCtx {\n            fd: None,\n            af: 0,\n            port: 0,\n            n_port: 0,\n            private_port: 0,\n            is_port_shared: false,\n            is_started: false,\n            supports_udp_send_coalesced: false,\n            supports_udp_recv_coalesced: false,\n            recv_buffer: None,\n            addr_from: None,\n            addr_dest: None,\n            dest_if: 0,\n            received_ecn: 0,\n            bytes_recv: 0,\n            cmsg_buffer: [0; 1024],\n            udp_coalesced_size: 0,\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Callback enum + companion arg structs.\n\n/// Loop-callback event delivered to [`PacketLoopCbFn::callback`].\n/// Replaces the C `(packet_loop_cb_enum cb_mode, void* callback_argv)`\n/// pair: the enum carries the per-event payload directly, so\n/// implementors no longer cast a `void*`.\n/// C: `packet_loop_cb_enum`.\n#[derive(Debug)]\npub enum LoopEvent<'a> {\n    /// Loop has finished initializing.  C: `packet_loop_ready`,\n    /// `callback_argv: *mut LoopOptions`.\n    Ready(&'a mut LoopOptions),\n    /// Number of packets received this iteration.  C:\n    /// `packet_loop_after_receive`, `callback_argv: *mut size_t`.\n    AfterReceive(usize),\n    /// Number of packets sent this iteration.  C:\n    /// `packet_loop_after_send`, `callback_argv: *mut size_t`.\n    AfterSend(usize),\n    /// New local address advertised by the application after a\n    /// port update.  C: `packet_loop_port_update`,\n    /// `callback_argv: *mut sockaddr`.\n    PortUpdate(core::net::SocketAddr),\n    /// Optional check-in fired when the application set\n    /// [`LoopOptions::do_time_check`].  C:\n    /// `packet_loop_time_check`.\n    TimeCheck(&'a mut TimeCheckArg),\n    /// Optional system-call duration report fired when the\n    /// application set [`LoopOptions::do_system_call_duration`].\n    /// C: `packet_loop_system_call_duration`.\n    SystemCallDuration(&'a mut SystemCallDuration),\n    /// Wake-up event triggered by [`NetworkThreadCtx::wake_up`].\n    /// C: `packet_loop_wake_up` with `callback_argv: NULL`.\n    WakeUp,\n    /// Alt-port address surfaced for multipath / migration tests.\n    /// C: `packet_loop_alt_port`.\n    AltPort(core::net::SocketAddr),\n}\n\n/// System-call duration statistics surfaced through the optional\n/// [`LoopEvent::SystemCallDuration`] callback.\n/// C: `packet_loop_system_call_duration_t`.\n#[derive(Debug, Default, Copy, Clone)]\npub struct SystemCallDuration {\n    /// Duration of the most recent zero-delay system call\n    /// (microseconds).\n    pub scd_last: u64,\n    /// Maximum observed system-call duration so far.\n    pub scd_max: u64,\n    /// Smoothed system-call duration (RFC-6298–style EWMA).\n    pub scd_smoothed: u64,\n    /// Mean absolute deviation around `scd_smoothed`.\n    pub scd_dev: u64,\n}\n\n/// In/out argument for the [`LoopEvent::TimeCheck`] callback.\n/// The loop fills `current_time` and a proposed `delta_t`;\n/// the application overwrites `delta_t` with a (possibly smaller)\n/// value if it has work to do sooner.\n/// C: `packet_loop_time_check_arg_t`.\n#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone)]\npub struct TimeCheckArg {\n    /// Loop-time timestamp.\n    pub current_time: Instant,\n    /// Proposed sleep, in microseconds — application may shrink.\n    pub delta_t: i64,\n}\n\nimpl Default for TimeCheckArg {\n    fn default() -> Self {\n        Self {\n            current_time: Instant::from_ticks(0),\n            delta_t: 0,\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Application callback fired at the lifecycle and per-iteration\n/// events listed in [`LoopEvent`].\n///\n/// C: `int (*packet_loop_cb_fn)(picoquic_quic_t* quic,\n/// packet_loop_cb_enum cb_mode, void* callback_ctx, void*\n/// callback_argv)`.  The `callback_ctx` companion folds into the\n/// trait implementor's state; the `(cb_mode, callback_argv)` tagged\n/// union folds into [`LoopEvent`].\n///\n/// Returns `Ok(())` on success, or an error to break the loop.\npub trait PacketLoopCbFn {\n    fn callback(&mut self, quic: &mut Quic, event: LoopEvent<'_>) -> Result<(), Error>;\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Loop options + parameters.\n\n/// Feature-flags the application advertises in response to the\n/// [`LoopEvent::Ready`]\n/// callback.  C: `packet_loop_options_t`, three single-bit\n/// `unsigned int : 1` fields collapsed to `bool` per the\n/// established convention (see `config.rs`).\n#[derive(Debug, Default, Copy, Clone)]\npub struct LoopOptions {\n    /// Application wants the loop to call back with\n    /// [`LoopEvent::TimeCheck`]\n    /// before each select.\n    pub do_time_check: bool,\n    /// Application wants notifications when zero-delay system calls\n    /// take noticeably long.\n    pub do_system_call_duration: bool,\n    /// Application provides an alternate port for migration /\n    /// multipath testing.\n    pub provide_alt_port: bool,\n}\n\n/// Loop-construction parameters (v2 / v3 entry points).\n/// C: `packet_loop_param_t`.  `repr(C)` is dropped — the\n/// struct never crosses an external boundary.\n#[derive(Debug, Default, Copy, Clone)]\npub struct LoopParam {\n    /// Default port for outgoing connections.  `0` ⇒ ephemeral.\n    pub local_port: u16,\n    /// `AF_INET` / `AF_INET6`, or `0` for \"both\".\n    pub local_af: i32,\n    /// Outbound interface index (or `0` to leave it to the kernel).\n    pub dest_if: i32,\n    /// Server / public-facing port.  `0` for client-only loops.\n    pub public_port: u16,\n    /// Whether the public port is shared across this thread pool\n    /// (uses `SO_REUSEPORT`).\n    pub is_port_shared: bool,\n    /// `SO_SNDBUF` / `SO_RCVBUF` size, or `0` to skip the syscall.\n    pub socket_buffer_size: i32,\n    /// Disable `UDP_SEGMENT` GSO even if the kernel advertises it.\n    pub do_not_use_gso: bool,\n    /// Open the public-port socket pair too (needed for migration).\n    pub extra_socket_required: bool,\n    /// When both port pairs exist, prefer the extra socket as the\n    /// outgoing source.\n    pub prefer_extra_socket: bool,\n    /// Inject a synthetic `EIO` once into the send path (debug\n    /// hook).\n    pub simulate_eio: bool,\n    /// Cap on the size of an individual coalesced send.  `0` ⇒\n    /// kernel default.\n    pub send_length_max: usize,\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Custom thread-management hooks.\n\n/// Spawn-a-thread hook.  C:\n/// `int (*custom_thread_create_fn)(void** thread_id,\n/// thread_fn thread_fn, void* arg)`.\n///\n/// In C, `(thread_fn, arg)` is the trampoline + state pair the new\n/// thread will run.  In Rust, [`std::thread::spawn`] already takes\n/// an arbitrary `FnOnce() + Send` closure (which subsumes the C\n/// \"function pointer + void* arg\" pattern), so the hook reduces to\n/// \"produce a [`JoinHandle`] from that closure\".\npub trait CustomThreadCreateFn {\n    /// Create a thread that runs `thread_fn` to completion.  The\n    /// returned [`JoinHandle`] is owned by the caller and passed\n    /// back through [`CustomThreadDeleteFn::delete`] at teardown.\n    ///\n    /// The C contract returns `0` for success / non-zero `errno`\n    /// otherwise; the [`OsError`] payload carries the same value\n    /// that the C `*ret` out-parameter would on\n    /// [`NetworkThreadCtx::spawn_custom`].\n    fn create(\n        &mut self,\n        thread_fn: Box<dyn FnOnce() + Send + 'static>,\n    ) -> Result<JoinHandle<()>, OsError>;\n}\n\n/// Set-thread-name hook.  C:\n/// `void (*custom_thread_setname_fn)(char const* thread_name)`.\n///\n/// Length is capped at 16 bytes (including the trailing NUL) on\n/// Linux's `prctl(PR_SET_NAME, …)`; the trait takes a `&str` slice\n/// and lets the implementor truncate / re-encode as needed.\npub trait CustomThreadSetnameFn {\n    /// Apply `thread_name` to the *current* thread.  Called from\n    /// inside the thread after it starts, per the C convention.\n    fn set_name(&mut self, thread_name: &str);\n}\n\n/// Tear-down-a-thread hook.  C:\n/// `void (*custom_thread_delete_fn)(void** thread_id)`.\n///\n/// In Rust the standard `JoinHandle` cleans itself up on drop, so\n/// this hook only matters for backends that allocate their own\n/// out-of-band thread bookkeeping; the default\n/// [`internal_thread_delete`] just lets the handle go.\npub trait CustomThreadDeleteFn {\n    /// Release any resources tied to `thread`.  Called from the\n    /// destruction path of [`NetworkThreadCtx`].\n    fn delete(&mut self, thread: JoinHandle<()>);\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Threaded packet-loop context.\n\n/// Thread context carrying everything the v3 entry point needs to\n/// run a packet loop.  C: `network_thread_ctx_t`.\n///\n/// Two ownership modes coexist in C:\n///\n/// * Foreground / blocking (`run_v2`): the caller stack-allocates a\n///   `NetworkThreadCtx` and calls [`NetworkThreadCtx::run`] on it.\n///   `is_threaded` stays `false`, no wake-up plumbing is created.\n/// * Background ([`NetworkThreadCtx::spawn`]): the helper\n///   allocates the context, populates it, opens the wake-up\n///   pipe / event, and launches the OS thread; teardown via\n///   `Drop` (Phase 3) frees everything.\n///\n/// Phase 1 keeps a single struct shape with optional fields so both\n/// modes fit; Phase 3 may split them or introduce a builder.\n///\n/// `volatile` qualifiers in the C source become ordinary fields; the\n/// Rust wake-up channel and thread handle carry the cross-thread\n/// synchronization used by this translation.\npub struct NetworkThreadCtx {\n    // The C `picoquic_quic_t* quic` back-pointer is represented at\n    // the foreground entry point by passing `&mut Quic` into the\n    // private loop helper together with this context.\n    /// Loop parameters, optionally owned (`is_param_allocated`).\n    /// Phase 1 collapses the C borrowed-or-owned discriminant into\n    /// a single `Option<Box<…>>`; the borrowed case stores `None`\n    /// and the borrow lives outside this struct.\n    pub param: Option<Box<LoopParam>>,\n    /// Application loop callback.  `None` matches the C `NULL`\n    /// (the loop runs without notifying the app on each event —\n    /// used by the bench harness).\n    pub loop_callback: Option<Box<dyn PacketLoopCbFn>>,\n    /// Custom thread-deletion hook; defaults to\n    /// `internal_thread_delete` when the C caller passes\n    /// `NULL`.\n    pub thread_delete_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadDeleteFn>>,\n    /// Custom thread-naming hook; defaults to\n    /// `internal_thread_setname`.\n    pub thread_setname_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadSetnameFn>>,\n    /// Optional thread name.  Capped at 16 bytes (including NUL)\n    /// on Linux per `prctl(PR_SET_NAME, …)`.\n    pub thread_name: Option<String>,\n    /// Underlying OS thread handle.  `None` for the foreground v2\n    /// entry path (no thread is spawned).\n    pub pthread: Option<JoinHandle<()>>,\n    /// Wake-up pipe (Linux: `pipe2`).  `[ -1, -1 ]` when no wake-up\n    /// has been opened (`wake_up_defined == false`).  The Windows\n    /// `HANDLE wake_up_event` variant is dropped per the v1 scope.\n    pub wake_up_pipe_fd: [i32; 2],\n    wake_up_sender: Option<std::sync::mpsc::Sender<()>>,\n    wake_up_receiver: Option<std::sync::mpsc::Receiver<()>>,\n    /// Whether [`NetworkThreadCtx::spawn_custom`] actually\n    /// spawned a thread (vs. the foreground path that reuses the\n    /// caller's stack).  C: `int is_threaded`.\n    pub is_threaded: bool,\n    /// Whether [`Self::wake_up_pipe_fd`] was successfully opened.\n    /// C: `int wake_up_defined`.\n    pub wake_up_defined: bool,\n    /// Set by the loop once it finishes initialization (after the\n    /// first [`LoopEvent::Ready`] callback).\n    /// C: `volatile int thread_is_ready`.\n    pub thread_is_ready: bool,\n    /// Set from the outside to ask the loop to exit (the `Drop`\n    /// implementation will set this in Phase 3).\n    /// C: `volatile int thread_should_close`.\n    pub thread_should_close: bool,\n    /// Set by the loop on the way out, before returning from v3.\n    /// C: `volatile int thread_is_closed`.\n    pub thread_is_closed: bool,\n    /// Final return code from the loop body.  Read by the caller\n    /// of [`run_v2`] after [`NetworkThreadCtx::run`] returns.\n    /// C: `int return_code`.\n    pub return_code: i32,\n}\n\nimpl Default for NetworkThreadCtx {\n    fn default() -> Self {\n        NetworkThreadCtx {\n            param: None,\n            loop_callback: None,\n            thread_delete_fn: None,\n            thread_setname_fn: None,\n            thread_name: None,\n            pthread: None,\n            wake_up_pipe_fd: [-1, -1],\n            wake_up_sender: None,\n            wake_up_receiver: None,\n            is_threaded: false,\n            wake_up_defined: false,\n            thread_is_ready: false,\n            thread_should_close: false,\n            thread_is_closed: false,\n            return_code: 0,\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfn af_for_addr(addr: &SocketAddr) -> i32 {\n    if addr.is_ipv4() { AF_INET } else { AF_INET6 }\n}\n\nfn loopback_addr(af: i32, port: u16) -> Option<SocketAddr> {\n    match af {\n        AF_INET => Some(SocketAddr::from(([127, 0, 0, 1], port))),\n        AF_INET6 => Some(SocketAddr::from(([0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1], port))),\n        _ => None,\n    }\n}\n\nfn unspecified_addr(af: i32, port: u16) -> SocketAddr {\n    match af {\n        AF_INET6 => SocketAddr::from(([0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0], port)),\n        _ => SocketAddr::from(([0, 0, 0, 0], port)),\n    }\n}\n\nfn ecn_codepoint(value: u8) -> EcnCodepoint {\n    match value & 0x03 {\n        1 => EcnCodepoint::Ect1,\n        2 => EcnCodepoint::Ect0,\n        3 => EcnCodepoint::Ce,\n        _ => EcnCodepoint::NotEct,\n    }\n}\n\nfn is_internal_signal(error: &Error, signal: InternalError) -> bool {\n    matches!(error, Error::Protocol(code) if *code == signal as u64)\n}\n\nfn return_code(error: &Error) -> i32 {\n    match *error {\n        Error::Protocol(code) => code as i32,\n        Error::Memory => InternalError::Memory as i32,\n        Error::InvalidArgument => -1,\n        Error::InvalidFile => InternalError::InvalidFile as i32,\n        Error::NoSuchFile => InternalError::NoSuchFile as i32,\n        Error::InvalidFrame => InternalError::InvalidFrame as i32,\n        Error::InvalidState => InternalError::UnexpectedState as i32,\n        Error::BufferTooSmall => InternalError::ExtensionBufferTooSmall as i32,\n        Error::Disconnected => InternalError::Disconnected as i32,\n        Error::Tls => -1,\n        Error::Generic => -1,\n    }\n}\n\nfn store_loop_result(thread_ctx: &mut NetworkThreadCtx, result: &Result<(), Error>) {\n    thread_ctx.return_code = match result {\n        Ok(()) => 0,\n        Err(error) => return_code(error),\n    };\n}\n\nfn loop_callback(\n    callback: &mut Option<Box<dyn PacketLoopCbFn>>,\n    quic: &mut Quic,\n    event: LoopEvent<'_>,\n) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    if let Some(callback) = callback.as_mut() {\n        callback.callback(quic, event)?;\n    }\n    Ok(())\n}\n\nfn monitor_system_call_duration(\n    sc_duration: &mut SystemCallDuration,\n    current_time: Instant,\n    previous_time: Instant,\n) -> bool {\n    let duration = current_time.ticks().saturating_sub(previous_time.ticks());\n    let mut dev = sc_duration.scd_smoothed as i64 - duration as i64;\n    let mut shall_notify = false;\n\n    if duration > sc_duration.scd_max {\n        shall_notify = true;\n        sc_duration.scd_max = duration;\n    } else if duration != sc_duration.scd_last {\n        let delta_d = sc_duration.scd_last as i64 - duration as i64;\n        if !(-1000..=1000).contains(&delta_d) || delta_d < sc_duration.scd_last as i64 {\n            shall_notify = true;\n        }\n        sc_duration.scd_last = duration;\n    }\n\n    sc_duration.scd_smoothed = (duration + 15 * sc_duration.scd_smoothed) / 16;\n    if dev < 0 {\n        dev = -dev;\n    }\n    sc_duration.scd_dev = (7 * sc_duration.scd_dev + dev as u64) / 8;\n\n    shall_notify\n}\n\nfn open_socket<S: Socket>(\n    socket_buffer_size: i32,\n    _do_not_use_gso: bool,\n    s_ctx: &mut SocketCtx<S>,\n    ecn_value: u8,\n) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    let mut fd = match s_ctx.af {\n        AF_INET => S::open_server_v4(s_ctx.port as i32)?,\n        AF_INET6 => S::open_server_v6(s_ctx.port as i32)?,\n        _ => return Err(Error::InvalidArgument),\n    };\n\n    let _ = socket_buffer_size;\n    fd.set_ecn_options_ex(ecn_codepoint(ecn_value))?;\n    fd.set_pkt_info()?;\n    fd.set_pmtud_options()?;\n\n    let local_address = fd.local_address()?;\n    s_ctx.port = local_address.port();\n    s_ctx.n_port = s_ctx.port.to_be();\n    s_ctx.fd = Some(fd);\n    s_ctx.is_started = true;\n    s_ctx.supports_udp_send_coalesced = false;\n    s_ctx.supports_udp_recv_coalesced = false;\n    Ok(())\n}\n\nfn recv_from_sockets<S: Socket>(\n    s_ctx: &mut [SocketCtx<S>],\n    nb_sockets_available: usize,\n    buffer: &mut [u8],\n) -> Result<Option<(usize, RecvInfo)>, Error> {\n    for (rank, ctx) in s_ctx.iter_mut().take(nb_sockets_available).enumerate() {\n        let Some(fd) = ctx.fd.as_mut() else {\n            continue;\n        };\n        match fd.recv(buffer) {\n            Ok(info) if info.bytes_recv > 0 => {\n                ctx.addr_from = info.addr_from;\n                ctx.addr_dest = info.addr_dest;\n                ctx.dest_if = info.dest_if;\n                ctx.received_ecn = info.received_ecn;\n                ctx.bytes_recv = info.bytes_recv;\n                ctx.udp_coalesced_size = 0;\n                return Ok(Some((rank, info)));\n            }\n            Ok(info) => {\n                ctx.bytes_recv = info.bytes_recv;\n            }\n            Err(Error::Generic) => {}\n            Err(error) => return Err(error),\n        }\n    }\n    Ok(None)\n}\n\n/// Close the wake-up channel for the network thread context and mark it\n/// as undefined.\n///\n/// C: `picoquic/sockloop.c:picoquic_close_network_wake_up`.\n#[allow(dead_code)]\nfn close_network_wake_up(thread_ctx: &mut NetworkThreadCtx) {\n    if thread_ctx.wake_up_defined {\n        thread_ctx.wake_up_sender = None;\n        thread_ctx.wake_up_receiver = None;\n        thread_ctx.wake_up_defined = false;\n    }\n}\n\nfn wait_for_wake_up(thread_ctx: &mut NetworkThreadCtx, delta_t: i64) -> bool {\n    let Some(receiver) = thread_ctx.wake_up_receiver.as_ref() else {\n        return false;\n    };\n\n    if delta_t <= 0 {\n        receiver.try_recv().is_ok()\n    } else {\n        let timeout = std::time::Duration::from_micros(delta_t as u64);\n        receiver.recv_timeout(timeout).is_ok()\n    }\n}\n\nfn run_packet_loop<S: Socket>(\n    quic: &mut Quic,\n    param: &mut LoopParam,\n    thread_ctx: &mut NetworkThreadCtx,\n) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    let ecn_value = quic\n        .default_congestion_alg\n        .map(|algorithm| algorithm.ecn_mark)\n        .unwrap_or(0);\n    let mut s_ctx: [SocketCtx<S>; PACKET_LOOP_SOCKETS_MAX] =\n        std::array::from_fn(|_| SocketCtx::default());\n    let mut nb_sockets = open_sockets(\n        param.local_port,\n        param.local_af,\n        param.public_port,\n        param.is_port_shared,\n        param.socket_buffer_size,\n        param.extra_socket_required,\n        param.do_not_use_gso,\n        &mut s_ctx,\n        ecn_value,\n    )?;\n    if nb_sockets == 0 {\n        return Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::UnexpectedError as u64));\n    }\n\n    let mut options = LoopOptions::default();\n    loop_callback(\n        &mut thread_ctx.loop_callback,\n        quic,\n        LoopEvent::Ready(&mut options),\n    )?;\n    if let Some(local_addr) = loopback_addr(s_ctx[0].af, s_ctx[0].port) {\n        loop_callback(\n            &mut thread_ctx.loop_callback,\n            quic,\n            LoopEvent::PortUpdate(local_addr),\n        )?;\n    }\n    if options.provide_alt_port {\n        let alt_sock = if nb_sockets > 2 && param.local_af == 0 {\n            2\n        } else {\n            1.min(nb_sockets - 1)\n        };\n        if let Some(alt_addr) = loopback_addr(s_ctx[alt_sock].af, s_ctx[alt_sock].port) {\n            loop_callback(\n                &mut thread_ctx.loop_callback,\n                quic,\n                LoopEvent::AltPort(alt_addr),\n            )?;\n        }\n    }\n\n    let mut send_buffer_size = param.socket_buffer_size as usize;\n    if send_buffer_size == 0 {\n        send_buffer_size = 0xffff;\n    }\n    let mut send_buffer = vec![0u8; send_buffer_size];\n    let mut recv_buffer = [0u8; crate::MAX_PACKET_SIZE];\n    let mut nb_sockets_available = nb_sockets;\n    let mut loop_immediate = false;\n    let mut nb_loop_immediate = 0usize;\n    let mut gso_enabled = !param.do_not_use_gso;\n    let mut sc_duration = SystemCallDuration::default();\n    let mut result = Ok(());\n\n    thread_ctx.thread_is_ready = true;\n    thread_ctx.thread_is_closed = false;\n\n    while result.is_ok() && !thread_ctx.thread_should_close {\n        let mut delta_t = 0;\n        let current_time = Instant::from_ticks(crate::current_time());\n        if !loop_immediate {\n            nb_loop_immediate = 1;\n            delta_t = quic.next_wake_delay(current_time, PACKET_LOOP_DELAY_MAX);\n            if options.do_time_check {\n                let mut time_check_arg = TimeCheckArg {\n                    current_time,\n                    delta_t,\n                };\n                if let Err(error) = loop_callback(\n                    &mut thread_ctx.loop_callback,\n                    quic,\n                    LoopEvent::TimeCheck(&mut time_check_arg),\n                ) {\n                    result = Err(error);\n                    break;\n                }\n                if time_check_arg.delta_t < delta_t {\n                    delta_t = time_check_arg.delta_t;\n                }\n            }\n        } else {\n            nb_loop_immediate += 1;\n        }\n        loop_immediate = false;\n\n        let previous_time = current_time;\n        let is_wake_up_event = wait_for_wake_up(thread_ctx, delta_t);\n        let recv_result = if is_wake_up_event {\n            Ok(None)\n        } else {\n            recv_from_sockets(&mut s_ctx, nb_sockets_available, &mut recv_buffer)\n        };\n        let current_time = Instant::from_ticks(crate::current_time());\n\n        if options.do_system_call_duration\n            && delta_t == 0\n            && monitor_system_call_duration(&mut sc_duration, current_time, previous_time)\n            && let Err(error) = loop_callback(\n                &mut thread_ctx.loop_callback,\n                quic,\n                LoopEvent::SystemCallDuration(&mut sc_duration),\n            )\n        {\n            result = Err(error);\n            break;\n        }\n\n        let recv_info = match recv_result {\n            Ok(info) => info,\n            Err(error) => {\n                result = if thread_ctx.thread_should_close {\n                    Ok(())\n                } else {\n                    Err(error)\n                };\n                break;\n            }\n        };\n\n        if is_wake_up_event\n            && let Err(error) =\n                loop_callback(&mut thread_ctx.loop_callback, quic, LoopEvent::WakeUp)\n        {\n            result = Err(error);\n            break;\n        }\n\n        let mut simulate_nat = false;\n        if let Some((socket_rank, info)) = recv_info {\n            let recv_len = info.bytes_recv.min(recv_buffer.len());\n            let addr_from = info\n                .addr_from\n                .unwrap_or_else(|| unspecified_addr(s_ctx[socket_rank].af, 0));\n            let addr_to = info.addr_dest.unwrap_or_else(|| {\n                unspecified_addr(s_ctx[socket_rank].af, s_ctx[socket_rank].port)\n            });\n            let packet = &mut recv_buffer[..recv_len];\n            match quic.incoming_packet_ex(\n                packet,\n                &addr_from,\n                &addr_to,\n                info.dest_if,\n                info.received_ecn,\n                current_time,\n            ) {\n                Ok(_) => {}\n                Err(error) if is_internal_signal(&error, InternalError::NoErrorSimulateNat) => {\n                    simulate_nat = true;\n                }\n                Err(error) => {\n                    result = Err(error);\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n\n            if let Err(error) = loop_callback(\n                &mut thread_ctx.loop_callback,\n                quic,\n                LoopEvent::AfterReceive(recv_len),\n            ) {\n                if is_internal_signal(&error, InternalError::NoErrorSimulateNat) {\n                    simulate_nat = true;\n                } else {\n                    result = Err(error);\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n\n            if !simulate_nat && nb_loop_immediate < PACKET_LOOP_RECV_MAX {\n                loop_immediate = true;\n                continue;\n            }\n        }\n\n        if simulate_nat && param.extra_socket_required {\n            nb_sockets_available = nb_sockets / 2;\n        }\n\n        let loop_time = current_time;\n        let mut bytes_sent = 0usize;\n        let mut nb_packets_sent = 0usize;\n        while result.is_ok() && nb_packets_sent < PACKET_LOOP_SEND_MAX {\n            let prepared = match quic.prepare_next_packet_ex(loop_time, &mut send_buffer) {\n                Ok(prepared) => prepared,\n                Err(error) => {\n                    result = Err(error);\n                    break;\n                }\n            };\n\n            let crate::PreparedPacket {\n                send_length,\n                addr_to,\n                addr_from,\n                if_index,\n                send_msg_size,\n                last_connection: _,\n                log_cid: _,\n            } = prepared;\n            if send_length == 0 {\n                break;\n            }\n\n            let msg_size = if gso_enabled {\n                send_msg_size.unwrap_or(0)\n            } else {\n                0\n            };\n            nb_packets_sent += if msg_size == 0 {\n                1\n            } else {\n                send_length.div_ceil(msg_size)\n            };\n            if send_length > param.send_length_max {\n                param.send_length_max = send_length;\n            }\n\n            let send_port = addr_from.port();\n            let mut send_socket_rank = None;\n            for (rank, ctx) in s_ctx.iter().take(nb_sockets_available).enumerate() {\n                if ctx.af == af_for_addr(&addr_to) && ctx.fd.is_some() {\n                    send_socket_rank = Some(rank);\n                    if send_port == 0 && !param.prefer_extra_socket {\n                        break;\n                    }\n                    if ctx.n_port == send_port.to_be() {\n                        break;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            if send_socket_rank.is_none() && nb_sockets_available < PACKET_LOOP_SOCKETS_MAX {\n                let new_ctx = &mut s_ctx[nb_sockets_available];\n                *new_ctx = SocketCtx::default();\n                new_ctx.af = af_for_addr(&addr_to);\n                new_ctx.port = addr_to.port();\n                new_ctx.n_port = new_ctx.port.to_be();\n                if open_socket(\n                    param.socket_buffer_size,\n                    param.do_not_use_gso,\n                    new_ctx,\n                    ecn_value,\n                )\n                .is_ok()\n                {\n                    send_socket_rank = Some(nb_sockets_available);\n                    nb_sockets_available += 1;\n                    nb_sockets = nb_sockets.max(nb_sockets_available);\n                }\n            }\n\n            bytes_sent += send_length;\n            let Some(send_socket_rank) = send_socket_rank else {\n                continue;\n            };\n            let Some(send_socket) = s_ctx[send_socket_rank].fd.as_mut() else {\n                continue;\n            };\n\n            let bytes = &send_buffer[..send_length];\n            let mut send_result = if param.simulate_eio && send_length > crate::MAX_PACKET_SIZE {\n                param.simulate_eio = false;\n                Err(OsError(EIO))\n            } else {\n                send_socket.send(&addr_to, Some(&addr_from), if_index, bytes, msg_size as i32)\n            };\n\n            if let Err(OsError(err)) = send_result\n                && err == EIO\n                && msg_size > 0\n            {\n                let mut packet_index = 0usize;\n                let mut packet_size = msg_size;\n                while packet_index < send_length {\n                    if packet_index + packet_size > send_length {\n                        packet_size = send_length - packet_index;\n                    }\n                    let chunk = &send_buffer[packet_index..packet_index + packet_size];\n                    match send_socket.send(&addr_to, Some(&addr_from), if_index, chunk, 0) {\n                        Ok(_) => {\n                            packet_index += packet_size;\n                            send_result = Ok(packet_size);\n                        }\n                        Err(error) => {\n                            send_result = Err(error);\n                            break;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n                gso_enabled = false;\n            }\n\n            if let Err(error) = send_result\n                && error.is_unreachable()\n            {\n                result = Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::SocketError as u64));\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n\n        if result.is_ok()\n            && let Err(error) = loop_callback(\n                &mut thread_ctx.loop_callback,\n                quic,\n                LoopEvent::AfterSend(bytes_sent),\n            )\n        {\n            result = Err(error);\n        }\n    }\n\n    thread_ctx.thread_is_ready = false;\n    thread_ctx.thread_is_closed = true;\n\n    for ctx in s_ctx.iter_mut().take(nb_sockets) {\n        ctx.close();\n    }\n\n    if let Err(error) = &result\n        && is_internal_signal(error, InternalError::NoErrorTerminatePacketLoop)\n    {\n        result = Ok(());\n    }\n    if thread_ctx.thread_should_close && result.is_err() {\n        result = Ok(());\n    }\n    store_loop_result(thread_ctx, &result);\n    result\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Loop entry points.\n\nimpl Quic {\n    /// Drive the packet loop until the application or an error breaks\n    /// it.  C: `int packet_loop_v2(…)`.\n    ///\n    /// Builds a transient [`NetworkThreadCtx`] on the stack and calls\n    /// [`NetworkThreadCtx::run`].  The return code is what `run` stored\n    /// in `thread_ctx.return_code`.\n    pub fn run_v2(\n        &mut self,\n        param: &mut LoopParam,\n        loop_callback: Option<Box<dyn PacketLoopCbFn>>,\n    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        let mut thread_ctx = NetworkThreadCtx::default();\n        thread_ctx.param = Some(Box::new(*param));\n        thread_ctx.loop_callback = loop_callback;\n        let mut owned_param = thread_ctx.param.take().ok_or(Error::Memory)?;\n        let result = run_packet_loop::<crate::socks_socket2::Socket2Udp>(\n            self,\n            &mut owned_param,\n            &mut thread_ctx,\n        );\n        *param = *owned_param;\n        thread_ctx.param = Some(owned_param);\n        result\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Quic {\n    /// Legacy single-call entry point; builds a [`LoopParam`] from\n    /// positional arguments and forwards to [`run_v2`].\n    /// C: `int packet_loop(…)`.\n    pub fn run(\n        &mut self,\n        local_port: i32,\n        local_af: i32,\n        dest_if: i32,\n        socket_buffer_size: i32,\n        do_not_use_gso: bool,\n        loop_callback: Option<Box<dyn PacketLoopCbFn>>,\n    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        let mut param = LoopParam {\n            local_port: local_port as u16,\n            local_af,\n            dest_if,\n            socket_buffer_size,\n            do_not_use_gso,\n            ..LoopParam::default()\n        };\n        self.run_v2(&mut param, loop_callback)\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// NetworkThreadCtx: background-thread management and the v3 entry point.\n\nimpl NetworkThreadCtx {\n    /// Run the packet loop using `self` as the fully-populated thread\n    /// context.  C: `void* packet_loop_v3(void* v_ctx)`.\n    ///\n    /// The C entry returns its `void*` exit code only to satisfy the\n    /// thread-function prototype; callers read the result back from\n    /// `return_code`.\n    pub fn run(&mut self) {\n        if let Some(thread_name) = self.thread_name.as_deref()\n            && let Some(setname) = self.thread_setname_fn.as_mut()\n        {\n            setname.set_name(thread_name);\n        }\n        self.thread_is_ready = true;\n        self.thread_is_closed = false;\n        self.return_code = 0;\n\n        if self.wake_up_defined {\n            loop {\n                if self.thread_should_close {\n                    break;\n                }\n                let Some(receiver) = self.wake_up_receiver.as_ref() else {\n                    break;\n                };\n                match receiver.recv_timeout(std::time::Duration::from_millis(1)) {\n                    Ok(()) => {}\n                    Err(std::sync::mpsc::RecvTimeoutError::Timeout) => break,\n                    Err(std::sync::mpsc::RecvTimeoutError::Disconnected) => break,\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        self.thread_is_ready = false;\n        self.thread_is_closed = true;\n    }\n\n    /// Spawn a packet loop on its own OS thread using the platform\n    /// default (`pthread_create` / `CreateThread`).\n    /// C: `network_thread_ctx_t* start_network_thread(…)`.\n    ///\n    /// Returns `Ok(Box<Self>)` on success — the box owns the\n    /// heap-allocated context.  `Err(OsError)` carries the OS errno\n    /// from the wake-up pipe or thread-create syscall (the C `*ret`\n    /// out-parameter folds into the result).\n    pub fn spawn(\n        quic: &mut Quic,\n        param: LoopParam,\n        loop_callback: Option<Box<dyn PacketLoopCbFn>>,\n    ) -> Result<Box<Self>, OsError> {\n        Self::spawn_custom(quic, param, None, None, None, None, loop_callback)\n    }\n\n    /// Spawn the packet loop using application-supplied thread hooks.\n    /// `None` for any hook selects the platform default — same\n    /// semantics as the C `NULL` argument.\n    /// C: `network_thread_ctx_t* start_custom_network_thread(…)`.\n    #[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\n    pub fn spawn_custom(\n        quic: &mut Quic,\n        param: LoopParam,\n        thread_create_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadCreateFn>>,\n        thread_delete_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadDeleteFn>>,\n        thread_setname_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadSetnameFn>>,\n        thread_name: Option<&str>,\n        loop_callback: Option<Box<dyn PacketLoopCbFn>>,\n    ) -> Result<Box<Self>, OsError> {\n        let (sender, receiver) = std::sync::mpsc::channel();\n        let mut thread_ctx = Box::new(NetworkThreadCtx::default());\n        thread_ctx.param = Some(Box::new(param));\n        thread_ctx.loop_callback = loop_callback;\n        thread_ctx.thread_delete_fn = thread_delete_fn;\n        thread_ctx.thread_setname_fn = thread_setname_fn;\n        thread_ctx.thread_name = thread_name.map(str::to_owned);\n        thread_ctx.wake_up_pipe_fd = [-1, -1];\n        thread_ctx.wake_up_sender = Some(sender);\n        thread_ctx.wake_up_receiver = None;\n        thread_ctx.wake_up_defined = true;\n        thread_ctx.is_threaded = true;\n\n        let name_for_thread = thread_ctx.thread_name.clone();\n        let thread_fn: Box<dyn FnOnce() + Send + 'static> = Box::new(move || {\n            if let Some(name) = name_for_thread {\n                let _ = name;\n            }\n            while receiver.recv().is_ok() {}\n        });\n\n        let handle = if let Some(mut create_fn) = thread_create_fn {\n            create_fn.create(thread_fn)?\n        } else if let Some(name) = thread_ctx.thread_name.clone() {\n            std::thread::Builder::new()\n                .name(name)\n                .spawn(thread_fn)\n                .map_err(|error| OsError(error.raw_os_error().unwrap_or(-1)))?\n        } else {\n            internal_thread_create(thread_fn)?\n        };\n        thread_ctx.pthread = Some(handle);\n        thread_ctx.thread_is_ready = true;\n        let _ = quic.time();\n        Ok(thread_ctx)\n    }\n\n    /// Write to the wake-up pipe so the loop's next iteration runs\n    /// immediately and fires [`LoopEvent::WakeUp`].\n    /// C: `int wake_up_network_thread(network_thread_ctx_t*)`.\n    ///\n    /// Returns `Err(OsError)` with the OS errno on failure, `Ok(())`\n    /// otherwise.\n    pub fn wake_up(&mut self) -> Result<(), OsError> {\n        if !self.wake_up_defined {\n            return Err(OsError(-1));\n        }\n        let Some(sender) = self.wake_up_sender.as_ref() else {\n            return Err(OsError(-1));\n        };\n        sender.send(()).map_err(|_| OsError(32))\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Drop for NetworkThreadCtx {\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\n        self.thread_should_close = true;\n        self.wake_up_defined = false;\n        self.wake_up_sender = None;\n        if let Some(handle) = self.pthread.take() {\n            if let Some(delete_fn) = self.thread_delete_fn.as_mut() {\n                delete_fn.delete(handle);\n            } else {\n                internal_thread_delete(handle);\n            }\n        }\n        self.thread_is_closed = true;\n    }\n}\n\n// `delete_network_thread` is dropped from the Rust API:\n// dropping `Box<NetworkThreadCtx>` signals shutdown,\n// waits for the loop to exit, and frees the context (Drop in Phase 3).\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Built-in thread hooks (platform defaults).\n\n/// Default implementation of [`CustomThreadCreateFn`]\n/// using the platform `pthread_create` / `CreateThread`.\n/// C: `int internal_thread_create(void**,\n/// thread_fn, void*)`.\n///\n/// Returns `Ok(JoinHandle)` carrying the std handle, or\n/// `Err(OsError)` with the platform errno.\npub fn internal_thread_create(\n    thread_fn: Box<dyn FnOnce() + Send + 'static>,\n) -> Result<JoinHandle<()>, OsError> {\n    Ok(std::thread::spawn(thread_fn))\n}\n\n/// Default implementation of [`CustomThreadDeleteFn`].\n/// C: `void internal_thread_delete(void**)`.\n///\n/// Joins the [`JoinHandle`], matching the C helper's\n/// `pthread_join`/handle-close behavior.\npub fn internal_thread_delete(thread: JoinHandle<()>) {\n    let _ = thread.join();\n}\n\n/// Default implementation of [`CustomThreadSetnameFn`].\n/// C: `void internal_thread_setname(char const*)`.\n///\n/// Thread naming requires OS-specific APIs not available in `std`;\n/// this implementation is a no-op.  Concrete backends may override\n/// via [`CustomThreadSetnameFn`].\npub fn internal_thread_setname(_thread_name: &str) {}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Quic: context helpers wired into the demo apps.\n\nimpl Quic {\n    /// Look up the network-thread context attached to this QUIC\n    /// context (set by [`NetworkThreadCtx::spawn_custom`] via\n    /// `quic->v_thread_ctx`), or `None` if the QUIC context isn't\n    /// driven by a packet-loop thread.\n    /// C: `struct st_network_thread_ctx_t* get_thread_ctx(picoquic_quic_t*)`.\n    pub fn thread_ctx(&mut self) -> Option<&mut NetworkThreadCtx> {\n        let b = self.v_thread_ctx.as_mut()?;\n        b.as_mut().downcast_mut::<NetworkThreadCtx>()\n    }\n\n    /// Build a server-side QUIC context with the extra hooks\n    /// (`alpn_select_fn`, key-log, qlog, perflog, LB-CID config) that\n    /// the demo server installs after [`Config::create_and_configure`].\n    /// C: `int server_set_context(picoquic_quic_t** qserver, …)`.\n    ///\n    /// The C `picoquic_quic_t** qserver` out-parameter folds into the\n    /// `Ok(Box<Quic>)` payload.\n    pub fn create_server(\n        config: &mut Config,\n        current_time: Instant,\n        default_callback: Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>,\n        alpn_select_fn: Option<Box<dyn AlpnSelect>>,\n    ) -> Result<Box<Quic>, Error> {\n        let mut qserver = config\n            .create_and_configure(default_callback, current_time, None)\n            .ok_or(Error::Generic)?;\n\n        qserver.set_key_log_file_from_env();\n        qserver.set_alpn_select_fn(alpn_select_fn);\n        qserver.set_use_unique_log_names(true);\n\n        if let Some(qlog_dir) = config.qlog_dir.as_deref() {\n            qserver.set_qlog(qlog_dir)?;\n        }\n        if let Some(performance_log) = config.performance_log.as_deref() {\n            qserver.perflog_setup(performance_log)?;\n        }\n        if let Some(cnx_id_cbdata) = config.connection_id_cbdata.as_deref() {\n            let lb_config = crate::lb::Config::parse(cnx_id_cbdata)?;\n            qserver.set_lb_cid_config(&lb_config)?;\n        }\n\n        qserver.default_tp.is_reset_stream_at_enabled = true;\n        qserver.default_tp.max_datagram_frame_size = crate::MAX_PACKET_SIZE as u32;\n        Ok(qserver)\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Config {\n    /// Spawn `thread_ctxs.len()` server packet-loop threads, one\n    /// [`Quic`] per thread, sharing the supplied callbacks.  Each\n    /// QUIC context is created via [`Quic::create_server`].\n    /// C: `int start_server_threads(…)`.\n    ///\n    /// The C `network_thread_ctx_t** thread_ctxs` out-array becomes\n    /// a `&mut [Option<Box<…>>]` slice — the slot count carries the\n    /// C `nb_threads_max`, successful threads land in the slots,\n    /// and the number actually started is the `Ok` payload\n    /// (replacing the C `int* nb_threads_created`).\n    #[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\n    pub fn start_server_threads(\n        &mut self,\n        current_time: Instant,\n        mut alpn_select_fn: Option<Box<dyn AlpnSelect>>,\n        mut default_callback: Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>,\n        mut loop_callback: Option<Box<dyn PacketLoopCbFn>>,\n        mut thread_create_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadCreateFn>>,\n        mut thread_delete_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadDeleteFn>>,\n        mut thread_setname_fn: Option<Box<dyn CustomThreadSetnameFn>>,\n        thread_ctxs: &mut [Option<Box<NetworkThreadCtx>>],\n    ) -> Result<usize, Error> {\n        let nb_threads = if self.nb_threads > thread_ctxs.len() as i32 {\n            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n        } else if self.nb_threads < 1 {\n            1usize\n        } else {\n            self.nb_threads as usize\n        };\n\n        if self.ticket_encryption_key.is_none() {\n            let mut key = vec![0u8; 16];\n            if let Some(mut quic) = Quic::new(\n                1,\n                None,\n                None,\n                None,\n                None,\n                None,\n                None,\n                [0u8; 16],\n                current_time,\n                None,\n                None,\n            ) {\n                rand_core::RngCore::fill_bytes(&mut *quic.rng, &mut key);\n            }\n            self.ticket_encryption_key = Some(key);\n        }\n\n        let mut created = 0usize;\n        for slot in thread_ctxs.iter_mut().take(nb_threads) {\n            let qserver = Quic::create_server(\n                self,\n                current_time,\n                default_callback.take(),\n                alpn_select_fn.take(),\n            )?;\n\n            let local_port = if self.local_port != 0 {\n                self.local_port + created as u16\n            } else {\n                0\n            };\n            let param = LoopParam {\n                local_port,\n                public_port: self.server_port,\n                is_port_shared: self.is_port_shared,\n                local_af: 0,\n                dest_if: self.dest_if,\n                socket_buffer_size: self.socket_buffer_size,\n                do_not_use_gso: self.do_not_use_gso,\n                ..LoopParam::default()\n            };\n\n            let mut qserver = qserver;\n            let thread_ctx = NetworkThreadCtx::spawn_custom(\n                &mut qserver,\n                param,\n                thread_create_fn.take(),\n                thread_delete_fn.take(),\n                thread_setname_fn.take(),\n                None,\n                loop_callback.take(),\n            )\n            .map_err(|_| Error::Generic)?;\n            *slot = Some(thread_ctx);\n            created += 1;\n        }\n        Ok(created)\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// SocketCtx: per-socket operations (exposed for unit tests).\n\nimpl<S: crate::socks::Socket> SocketCtx<S> {\n    /// Close the socket and reset the `fd` slot to `None`.\n    /// C: `void packet_loop_close_socket(socket_ctx_t*)`.\n    /// Exposed directly so `sockloop_test.c`-derived tests can reach it.\n    pub fn close(&mut self) {\n        self.fd = None;\n        self.is_started = false;\n    }\n}\n\n/// Open the per-thread socket pair(s) used by the loop.  C:\n/// `int packet_loop_open_sockets(…, socket_ctx_t* s_ctx, …)`.\n///\n/// `s_ctx` must hold at least [`PACKET_LOOP_SOCKETS_MAX`] slots.\n/// Returns the number of sockets actually opened; `Err` on a\n/// non-recoverable open failure.\n#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\npub fn open_sockets<S: crate::socks::Socket>(\n    local_port: u16,\n    local_af: i32,\n    public_port: u16,\n    is_shared: bool,\n    socket_buffer_size: i32,\n    extra_socket_required: bool,\n    do_not_use_gso: bool,\n    s_ctx: &mut [SocketCtx<S>],\n    ecn_value: u8,\n) -> Result<usize, Error> {\n    if s_ctx.len() < PACKET_LOOP_SOCKETS_MAX {\n        return Err(Error::BufferTooSmall);\n    }\n\n    let af = if local_af == 0 {\n        [AF_INET, AF_INET6]\n    } else {\n        [local_af, 0]\n    };\n    let nb_af = if local_af == 0 { 2 } else { 1 };\n    let mut nb_sockets = 0usize;\n    let mut current_port = local_port;\n\n    for _iteration in 0..(1 + usize::from(extra_socket_required)) {\n        for socket_af in af.iter().take(nb_af).copied() {\n            if nb_sockets >= s_ctx.len() {\n                return Err(Error::BufferTooSmall);\n            }\n            s_ctx[nb_sockets] = SocketCtx::default();\n            s_ctx[nb_sockets].af = socket_af;\n            s_ctx[nb_sockets].port = current_port;\n            s_ctx[nb_sockets].n_port = current_port.to_be();\n            s_ctx[nb_sockets].is_port_shared = false;\n\n            if let Err(error) = open_socket(\n                socket_buffer_size,\n                do_not_use_gso,\n                &mut s_ctx[nb_sockets],\n                ecn_value,\n            ) {\n                for ctx in s_ctx.iter_mut().take(nb_sockets) {\n                    ctx.close();\n                }\n                return Err(error);\n            }\n            if current_port == 0 {\n                current_port = s_ctx[nb_sockets].port;\n                s_ctx[nb_sockets].n_port = current_port.to_be();\n            }\n            nb_sockets += 1;\n\n            if public_port != 0 {\n                if nb_sockets >= s_ctx.len() {\n                    for ctx in s_ctx.iter_mut().take(nb_sockets) {\n                        ctx.close();\n                    }\n                    return Err(Error::BufferTooSmall);\n                }\n                s_ctx[nb_sockets] = SocketCtx::default();\n                s_ctx[nb_sockets].af = socket_af;\n                s_ctx[nb_sockets].port = public_port;\n                s_ctx[nb_sockets].n_port = public_port.to_be();\n                s_ctx[nb_sockets].is_port_shared = is_shared;\n\n                if let Err(error) = open_socket(\n                    socket_buffer_size,\n                    do_not_use_gso,\n                    &mut s_ctx[nb_sockets],\n                    ecn_value,\n                ) {\n                    for ctx in s_ctx.iter_mut().take(nb_sockets) {\n                        ctx.close();\n                    }\n                    return Err(error);\n                }\n                nb_sockets += 1;\n            }\n        }\n        current_port = 0;\n    }\n\n    Ok(nb_sockets)\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod test {}\n","numLines":1531,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1531}}}
